      desc = Agaricus subrufescens (almond mushroom, almond agaricus, mushroom of the sun, God's mushroom, mushroom of life, royal sun agaricus, jisongrong (Chinese), himematsutake (Japanese)). A white mushroom with pink gills and creamy-brown-dappled cap.  Originally described from the northeastern U.S. and Canada, it has been found growing in California, Hawaii, Great Britain, the Netherlands, Taiwan, Philippines, Iran, Australia, Brazil, and Uruguay.
    {Mushroom^0.5|Agaricus}^[((Base == "CinnamonTort" || Base == "Cinnamon") && Silver && Agouti == "Tabby") && (NorthAm || Japan || Australia || NewZeal)]
      desc = Agaricus subrutilescens (wine-colored agaricus). Light brown mushroom with a white stem. Found in North America and Japan, though recently reported from Australia and New Zealand.
