      desc = Agaricus xanthodermus (yellow-staining agaricus, yellow-staining mushroom, yellow-stainer). A mostly white mushroom, sometimes with a dark grey spot on the cap, or yellow stains. Widely distributed in North America, Europe, West Asia including eastern Anatolia and Iran, North Africa, and southern Africa. It has been introduced into Australia.
    
