    {Mushroom^0.5|Fairyfingers|Coral|Spindles}^[(Base == "White") && (NorthAm || Europe || British || SouthAf || WestAs || EastAs || SEastAs || Australia)]
      desc = Clavaria fragilis (fairy fingers, white worm coral, or white spindles). A white coral fungus, growing as clusters of white tendrils. The species occurs throughout the Northern Hemisphere, in Europe, North America, and Asia. In North America, it is more common east of the Rocky Mountains. It has also been recorded from Australia and South Africa. It was reported from the Arctic zone of the Ural Mountains, in Russia.
    {Mushroom^0.5|Fairyclub|Club|Clavaria|Spindles}^[(Base == "White") && (NorthAm || Europe || British)]
