      desc = Clavulinopsis aurantiocinnabarina (orange spindle coral, orange worm coral). A bright yellow coral fungus growing in tendrils. First found in Pennsylvania (USA), its distribution in North America is unclear. Also found in Central America and the Caribbean, Brazil, China, and Malaysia.
    {Mushroom^0.5|Coral}^[(((Base == "Red" && Rufous == "Low") || (Base == "Cream" && Rufous == "High")) && White == "NoWhite" && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || MidAm || SouthAm || Europe || British || NorthAf || SouthAf || WestAs || EastAs || SEastAs || Australia)]
      desc = Clavulinopsis corniculata (meadow coral). A yellow coral fungus growing in tendrils. First found in Pennsylvania (USA), its distribution in North America is unclear. It is widely distributed throughout Europe, but has also been reported from North America, Central and South America, Africa, Asia, and Australia.
