      desc = Clavulinopsis fusiformis (golden spindles, spindle-shaped yellow coral, golden fairy spindle). A bright yellow coral fungus growing in tendrils. The species was initially described from England and is common throughout Europe. Has been reported from North America, Central and South America, and Asia, including Iran, China, Nepal, and Japan.
    {Mushroom^0.5|Club}^[(((Base == "Red" && Rufous == "Low") || (Base == "Cream" && Rufous == "High")) && White == "NoWhite" && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || SouthAm || Europe || British || EastAs || Japan)]
