      desc = Clavulinopsis laeticolor (golden fairy club, handsome club). A bright yellow coral fungus growing in tendrils. First described from Cuba, it's one of several similar species that can be hard to distinguish. In its wide sense, as part of a complex of similar species, it has been reported from North America, Europe (as C. pulchra), Malaya (as C. pulchra), China, Australia (as C. pulchra), New Zealand, Brazil, Central and South America (as C. pulchra).
    {Mushroom|Coral}^[(Base == "Red" && Rufous == "High" && White == "NoWhite" && Albino == "Normal") && (Australia || NewZeal)]
