      desc = Coprinellus micaceus (mica cap, glistening inky cap, shiny cap). A creamy orange mushroom that grows in clusters. Its stem is white and the gills may be black. Collected in northern Africa, South Africa, Europe (including Turkey), North America (as far north as Alaska), the Hawaiian islands, South America, India, Australia, New Zealand, and Japan.
