      desc = Cortinarius camphoratus (goatcheese webcap). A pale mushroom with pink gills. Found in Europe and North America.
    {Mushroom^0.5|Webcap}^[((Base == "Red") && (White == "MidWhite" || White == "HighWhite" || Albino != "Normal")) && (NorthAm || Europe || British || WestAs || Islands)]
      desc = Cortinarius caperatus. A pale brown mushroom with a light stem. It is found throughout northern Europe, mainly in Scandinavia, where it is common, although it is uncommon in Denmark and Iceland. In the British Isles it is uncommon outside the Scottish Highlands and the New Forest. It is widely found in northern parts of North America, as far south as Mendocino County on the west coast. It is a rare component of subarctic areas of western Greenland. The fungus also grows in temperate Asia, having been recorded near Pamukova in the Marmara Region of Turkey. It is also found in western Siberia.
