      desc = Crucibulum laeve (white-egg bird's nest). A brown bowl-shaped mushroom, with a yellow inside. The inside features hard discs containing spores which give it its name. It has been collected in most European countries and the Canary Islands; in North America it has been found from Alaska to Mexico, while South American locations include Chile and Tierra del Fuego. It has also been found in Australia, Iceland, Japan, and New Zealand.
