      desc = Entoloma sinuatum (livid entoloma, livid agaric, livid pinkgill, leaden entoloma, lead poisoner). A pale cream mushroom with a white stem. Widespread across North America as far south as Arizona. It also occurs throughout Europe and including Ireland and Britain, though it is more common in southern and central parts of Europe than the northwest. In Asia, it has been recorded in the Black Sea region, the Adıyaman Province in Turkey, Iran, and northern Yunnan in China.
