      desc = Favolaschia calocera (orange pore fungus, orange pore conch, orange Ping-Pong bat). A golden porous mushroom, it's known to be native to Madagascar. It's also found in other places sometimes as an invasive species, including New Zealand, Italy, Spain, Great Britain, Portugal, France, Switzerland, Belgium, Netherlands, Isle of Man, Venezuela, Brazil, Peru, Costa Rica, Hawaii, Australia, French Islands Réunion Island and Mayotte, Kenya, DR Congo, Tanzania, Zambia, the Seychelles, Thailand, China, India, Sumatra. It may actually be several similar species. 
