      desc = Aureoboletus moravicus (tawny bolete). Pale brown mushroom with yellow pores and pale stem. Across Europe, known from scattered localities in central and southern temperate regions.
    {Mushroom^0.5|Bolete}^[((Base == "CinnamonTort" || Base == "Cinnamon") && (White == "NoWhite" || White == "LowWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || Europe)]
      desc = Aureoboletus projectellus. Brown mushroom with yellow pores. In North America, its range includes eastern Canada (New Brunswick) south to North Carolina and west to Michigan. In Europe, it's been reported from Lithuania, Latvia, Estonia, Poland, Finland, Sweden, Denmark, and Norway.
    {Mushroom^0.5|Bolete}^[((Base == "Cream" || Base == "FawnTort") && White == "NoWhite" && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || MidAm || EastAs || Islands)]
      desc = Aureoboletus russellii (jagged-stemmed bolete, Russell's bolete). Pinkish cream mushroom with a ridged stem. The geographic range extends from eastern Canada south to Central America, and west to Michigan and southern Arizona. It is also found in Asia, including Korea and Taiwan.
    //Austroboletus
