      desc = Phlebopus marginatus (salmon gum mushroom). Dark brown mushroom with light pores. Found in Indonesia, Malaysia and Sri Lanka as well as Australia and New Zealand. Within Australia it has been recorded from the southeast of South Australia to New South Wales. It occurs in rainforest in the Cooloola section of the Great Sandy National Park in Queensland. It is common in Java and Sumatra. In China it is found in Yunnan, Guangxi and Hainan provinces.

