      desc = Gomphidius subroseus (rosy gomphidius, rosy slimespike). Pink mushroom with white stem. It is found in Europe and North America.

    //Gyroporus
    {Mushroom^0.5|Bolete}^[((Base == "Red") && Albino == "Normal" && (White == "LowWhite")) && (NorthAm || Europe || British)]
      desc = Gyroporus castaneus (chestnut bolete). Orange cap with a lighter stem and white pores.Found occasionally in Britain and throughout continental Europe, as well as eastern North America, but it is rare in western North America.
    {Mushroom^0.5|Bolete}^[(((Base == "Red" && Rufous == "Low") || (Base == "Cream" && Rufous == "High")) && Albino == "Normal" && (White == "LowWhite")) && (NorthAm || Europe || EastAs || Japan || Australia)]
      desc = Gyroporus cyanescens (bluing bolete, cornflower bolete). Yellow mushroom with white pores. Found in Europe, Asia, Australia, and North America. In China, it is known from Guangdong and Yunnan. Appears in eucalypt woodland in Australia. In North America, it is widespread east of the Rocky Mountains. The geographical distribution ranges from eastern Canada to Florida, and west to Minnesota, although it has been occasionally reported from the Pacific Northwest, and one collection has been made in the Sky Islands of southern Arizona. A variety has been reported from Japan.
    {Mushroom^0.5|Bolete}^[((Base == "Cream") && Albino == "Normal" && (White == "NoWhite")) && (MidAm)]
      desc = Gyroporus phaeocyanescens. Mottled cream mushroom found in Belize.
    {Mushroom^0.5|Bolete}^[((Base == "Cinnamon" || (Base == "Red" && Rufous == "High")) && Albino == "Normal" && (White == "LowWhite")) && (NorthAm)]
