      desc = Gyrodon lividus (alder bolete). Light yellow mushroom with pale stem. Found across Europe, including Ķemeri National Park in Latvia, In Asia, it has been recorded in China and Japan. It is also found in several locales in Turkey, including Trabzon, Maçka and Sevinç. In North America, it has been reported to occur in California.
    //Melanogaster
    Mushroom^[((Base == "BlueTort") && Albino == "Normal" && (White == "NoWhite")) && (NorthAm || Europe || British || Australia || NewZeal)]
      desc = Melanogaster ambiguus. Dark grey and yellow mushroom. It appears in North America, Oceania and Europe (according to GBIF).
    //Paragyrodon
    Mushroom^[((Base == "CinnamonTort" || Base == "Cinnamon") && Albino == "Normal" && (White == "NoWhite")) && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Paragyrodon sphaerosporus. Light brown mushroom. Distributed mostly around the Great Lakes Region, however, the species has also been observed further west in Kansas, Iowa and Colorado.
    //Paxillus
    {Mushroom^0.5|Roll-rim}^[((Base == "Cream" || Base == "Red" || Base == "Fawn" || Base == "FawnTort")) && (NorthAm || SouthAm || Europe || British || WestAs || EastAs || Japan || Australia || NewZeal || Islands)]
      desc = Paxillus involutus (brown roll-rim, common roll-rim). Pale brown or cream with a white stem. Found across the Northern Hemisphere, Europe and Asia, with records from India, China, Japan, Iran, and Turkey's eastern Anatolia. It is equally widely distributed across northern North America, extending north to Alaska. Recorded in southwestern Greenland. Reported as introduced in Australia, New Zealand, Chile.
    Mushroom^[((Base == "Red") && Albino == "Normal" && (White == "NoWhite")) && (NorthAm)]
