    {Mushroom|Truffle}^[((Base == "Cream") && Albino == "Normal" && (White == "NoWhite")) && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Rhizopogon occidentalis. Pale yellow mushroom found across western North America.
    {Mushroom|Truffle|Shōro^[if(Japan){1} else{0}]}^[((Base == "Red") && Albino == "Normal" && (White == "NoWhite")) && (NorthAm || Europe || Japan || NewZeal)]
      desc = Rhizopogon roseolus (shōro in Japan). Orange-brown mushroom. Distributed in Europe, North America and northeastern Asia. It has also been artificially introduced into New Zealand.
    {Mushroom|Truffle}^[((Base == "Cream") && (White == "HighWhite" || White == "MidWhite" || Albino == "Colourpoint")) && (NorthAm || Europe)]
      desc = Rhizopogon salebrosus. Pale yellow mushroom. Although it is native to North America, it has been found in Europe and its range is generally limited to mountainous regions.
    //Rhopalogaster
    Mushroom^[((Base == "Cream") && Albino == "Normal" && (White == "NoWhite" || White == "LowWhite")) && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Rhopalogaster transversarium. Pale cream mushroom found in the USA.
    //Calostoma
    {Mushroom^0.5|Puffball|Puffball-in-aspic|Stalked-puffball}^[((Base == "ChocolateTort") && Albino == "Normal" && (White == "NoWhite")) && (NorthAm || MidAm || SouthAm || EastAs || Japan || SEastAs || Islands)]
      desc = Calostoma cinnabarinum (red slimy-stalked puffball, stalked puffball-in-aspic, gelatinous stalked-puffball). Red mushroom with a brown stalk. Found from Massachusetts south to Florida in the United States. Its range extends at least as far west as Texas, with possible populations in the Southwest, but is most common in the Appalachian Mountains where it becomes more frequent with increasing elevation. It is also present in Eastern Mexico, where it grows in the subtropical cloud forests of Veracruz and Hidalgo. In Central America, it is known from Belize's Chiquibul National Park, the cloud forests of Baja Verapaz and El Quiché in Guatemala, and Panama. The species is also recorded in South America, from Colombia as far southeast as Brazil, where it is described as rare. It has also been collected from a disjunct population in Asia, where it has been recorded from seven provinces in mainland China, mostly in the southeast, as well as from Taiwan, Indonesia, Japan, and Jirisan in South Korea.
    Mushroom^[((Base == "BlackTort") && Albino == "Normal" && (White == "NoWhite")) && (Australia)]
      desc = Calostoma fuscum. Brown & black tangled-vines like mushroom with an orange bulb. Found in Australia.
    //Pisolithus
    {Mushroom^0.5|Dead-man's-foot|Dyeball|Pardebal|Truffle}^[((Base == "BlueTort") || (Base == "Blue" && (Albino == "Point" || White == "HighWhite"))) && (NorthAm || MidAm || SouthAm || Europe || British || SouthAf || EastAs || SEastAs || Japan || Hawaii)]
      desc = Pisolithus arhizus (dead man's foot, dyeball, pardebal, Bohemian truffle). Pale cream & dark grey round mushroom. Widespread fungus.
    //Scleroderma (earth balls)
    {Mushroom|Earthball}^[(Base == "White") && (NorthAm || MidAm || Islands)]
      desc = Scleroderma bermudense. White mushroom with a black inside. Indigenous to Bermuda, the Bahamas, Barbados, the Virgin Islands, Cuba, the Dominican Republic, Puerto Rico; the US state of Florida; and the Mexican states of Guerrero, Acapulco, Quintana Roo, Veracruz, and Yucatan. It has been introduced accidentally along with its host tree in various tropical regions, including French Guiana, Senegal, and Réunion.
    {Mushroom^0.5|Earthball}^[(((Base == "Red" && Rufous == "Low") || (Base == "Cream" && Rufous == "High") || (Gold != "None" && Agouti == "Tabby" && !Silver)) && Albino == "Normal" && (White == "NoWhite")) && (NorthAm || Europe || Australia)]
      desc = Scleroderma cepa (smooth earthball, onion earthball). Golden mushroom. It has a worldwide distribution and is especially common in North America, Europe, and Australia. It occurs throughout the United States, but is more abundant in the Eastern US.
    {Mushroom^0.5|Earthball|Puffball}^[((Base == "Cream") && Albino != "Point" && (White != "HighWhite")) && (NorthAm || Europe || British)]
      desc = Scleroderma citrinum (common earthball, pigskin poison puffball, common earth ball). Pale cream mushroom. Found in Europe and in North America, it is the most common species of earthball fungus in the United Kingdom.
    {Mushroom^0.5|Earthball}^[((Base == "Cream") && Albino == "Normal" && (White == "NoWhite")) && (Europe || WestAs || NorthAf)]
      desc = Scleroderma meridionale. Cream mushroom. Typically inhabits coastal and inland Mediterranean basin environments. Although originally described from southern Portugal, continental France, Corsica and Morocco, it is now recorded throughout the Mediterranean basin—including Greece, North Macedonia and Turkey.
    {Mushroom^0.5|Earthball|Dead-man's-hand}^[((Base == "Cream" || Base == "Red") && (Albino == "Normal" || Albino == "Sepia") && (White == "NoWhite" || White == "LowWhite")) && (NorthAm || SouthAm || Europe || British || NorthAf || SouthAf || EastAs || Japan || Islands)]
      desc = Scleroderma polyrhizum (star earthball, dead man's hand). Pale orange-brown mushroom with cream & white accents. It has a wide distribution in North America, including Mexico. It has also been recorded from Africa, Asia (China and Japan), Europe, South America (Brazil), and Oceania.
    {Mushroom^0.5|Earthball}^[((Base == "Cream") && (Tabby == "Spotted" || Tabby == "Ticked") && Albino == "Normal" && (White == "NoWhite")) && (NorthAm || SouthAm || Europe || NorthAf || SouthAf || EastAs || Australia || Hawaii)]
      desc = Scleroderma verrucosum. Dappled cream mushroom. Found in Africa, Asia (China and India), Australia, Europe, North America (including Hawaii), and South America.
    //Austropaxillus
    Mushroom^[(((Base == "Red" && Rufous == "Low") || (Base == "Cream" && Rufous == "High")) && Albino == "Normal" && (White == "NoWhite" || White == "LowWhite")) && (Australia)]
      desc = Austropaxillus infundibuliformis. Yellow mushroom found across southern Australia with records from Western Australia to Victoria and New South Wales.
    //Serpula
    Fungus^[((Base == "Red") && Albino == "Normal" && (White == "LowWhite" || White == "MidWhite")) && (NorthAm || MidAm || SouthAm || Europe || British || NorhtAf || SouthAf || WestAs || EastAs || Japan || SEastAs || Australia || NewZeal || Hawaii || Islands)]
      desc = Serpula himantioides. Orange and white fungus causing dry rot on trees. It has been found on all continents except for Antarctica.
    Fungus^[((Base == "Red") && Albino == "Normal" && (White == "LowWhite" || White == "MidWhite")) && (NorthAm || Europe || EastAs)]
      desc = Serpula lacrymans. Orange and white fungus causing dry rot on trees. Found naturally in the Himalayas, Northern California, the Czech Republic and east Asia.

    //Suillus
    {Mushroom^0.5|Suillus|Chickenfat}^[(((Base == "Red" && Rufous == "Low") || (Base == "Cream" && Rufous == "High"))) && (NorthAm || Europe || WestAs || EastAs || Japan)]
      desc = Suillus americanus (chicken fat mushroom, American suillus). Yellow mushroom found across North America, as well as across Europe and eastward across northern Asia, reaching Japan. Also found in the Himalayas.
    {Mushroom^0.5|Bolete}^[(Base == "White") && (Europe)]
      desc = Suillus bellinii (Champagne bolete). White mushroom found in southern Europe.
    {Mushroom^0.5|Bolete|Jerseycow}^[((Base == "CinnamonTort" || (Base == "Cinnamon" && Agouti != "Solid")) && Albino == "Normal" && (White == "NoWhite")) && (NorthAm || Europe || British || SouthAf || EastAs || Japan || Australia || NewZeal || Islands)]
      desc = Suillus bovinus (Jersey cow mushroom or bovine bolete). Brown mushroom with yellow pores. Found across Europe, including subalpine regions in the Alps, up to altitudes of 800 m (2500 ft). It is common in Lithuania. In Asia, it has been recorded in Taiwan, and in Japan. In China, it has been recorded from provinces Anhui, Fujian, Guangdong, Hunan, Jiangxi, and Zhejiang. Has been introduced into other areas. In North America, it is found in the eastern United States, including North Carolina, Pennsylvania, Vermont, and the Adirondack Mountains of New York. It has been recorded infrequently in Australia, where it has been found as far north as southern Queensland, and in more southerly locations including New South Wales and Kuitpo Forest. It has been recorded in New Zealand and South Africa.
    {Mushroom^0.5|Suillus}^[((Base == "CinnamonTort" || Base == "Cinnamon" || Base == "Red") && (Albino != "Normal" || White == "HighWhite")) && (Europe)]
      desc = Suillus bresadolae. White mushroom with a small round brown cap. Found in Europe.
    {Mushroom^0.5|Stubby-stalk|Jack}^[((Base == "Chocolate" || Base == "Cinnamon") && (Albino != "Normal" || White == "HighWhite" || White == "MidWhite")) && (NorthAm || MidAm || SouthAm || EastAs || Japan || NewZeal || Hawaii || Islands)]
      desc = Suillus brevipes (stubby-stalk, short-stemmed slippery Jack). Brown mushroom with pale yellow pores and white stem. It occurs over most of North America (including Hawaii), south to Mexico, and north to Canada. This species has been found in Puerto Rico, where it is thought to have been introduced inadvertently. Other introductions have also occurred in Argentina, India, New Zealand, Japan, and Taiwan.
    {Mushroom^0.5|Suillus|Jack}^[((Base == "Red") && Albino == "Normal" && (White == "NoWhite")) && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Suillus caerulescens (douglas-fir suillus, fat jack). Orange mushroom with golden pores. Found in western North America.
    {Mushroom^0.5|Hollowfoot}^[((Base == "Cinnamon" || Base == "Chocolate") && Albino == "Normal" && (White == "LowWhite" || White == "MidWhite")) && (NorthAm || Europe)]
