    {Mushroom^0.5|Suillus}^[(((Base == "Red" && Rufous == "Low") || (Base == "Cream" && Rufous == "High")) && (Albino == "Normal" || Albino == "Sepia") && (White == "LowWhite")) && (NorthAm || SouthAm || SEastAs)]
      desc = Suillus cothurnatus. Golden mushroom with a cream & white stem. In the United States, its range extends from Texas to Florida, and north to North Carolina. The species is also present in Mexico, and has been introduced to Brazil. It has also been recorded from the Cameron Highlands in Malaysia.
    {Mushroom^0.5|Suillus}^[((Base == "Red") && (Albino != "Normal" || White == "HighWhite" || White == "MidWhite")) && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Suillus decipiens. Orange mushroom with yellow pores and a pale stem. The fungus is found in southeastern North America, with the northern limit of its range extending to New Jersey.
    {Mushroom^0.5|Suillus}^[((Base == "Red" || Base == "Cream") && (Albino != "Normal" || White == "HighWhite" || White == "MidWhite")) && (Europe)]
