    {Mushroom^0.5|Bolete}^[((Base == "Red" || Base == "Cinnamon") && (Albino != "Normal" || White == "HighWhite" || White == "MidWhite")) && (SouthAm || Europe || British || NorthAf || SouthAf || EastAs || Australia || NewZeal || Hawaii)]
      desc = Suillus granulatus (weeping bolete, granulated bolete). Light brown mushroom with a white stem. It is common in Britain, Europe. It is found in South Korea. A native to the Northern Hemisphere, the fungus has been introduced into Australia. It is also found in Africa, New Zealand, Hawaii, Argentina and southern Chile.
    {Mushroom^0.5|Bolete|Jack}^[((Base == "Red" || Base == "CinnamonTort") && Albino == "Normal" && (White == "NoWhite")) && (NorthAm || Europe || Islands)]
      desc = Suillus grevillei (tamarack jack, Greville's bolete, larch bolete). Golden brown mushroom. Widespread in North America and Europe. In Asia, it has been recorded from Taiwan.
    {Mushroom^0.5|Suillus}^[((Base == "Red" || Base == "Cream") && (Albino != "Normal" || White == "HighWhite" || White == "MidWhite")) && (NorthAm || Europe)]
      desc = Suillus intermedius. Pale orange mushroom with pale stem found in North America and Costa Blanca Mountains, Spain.
    {Mushroom^0.5|Suillus}^[((Base == "Cream")) && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Suillus kaibabensis. Pale cream mushroom. Grows in the four corners region of Arizona, New Mexico, Utah, and Colorado.
    {Mushroom^0.5|Suillus}^[((Base == "CinnamonTort") && Albino == "Normal" && (White == "NoWhite")) && (EastAs)]
      desc = Suillus kunmingensis. Brown and light yellow mushroom with pale pores and stem. Found in China.
    {Mushroom^0.5|Suillus|Bolete|Jack}^[((Base == "Red") && Albino == "Normal" && (White == "NoWhite")) && (NorthAm || SouthAm || Europe || NewZeal)]
      desc = Suillus lakei (matte Jack, Lake's bolete, western painted Suillus). Golden brown mushroom. Indigenous to the Rocky Mountains and western parts of North America. Its range extends south into Mexico. Non-native introduced species in Europe.  These include Bosnia and Herzegovina, Bulgaria, Czech Republic, Germany, Hungary, Italy, and Slovakia. Has also been reported in South America (Argentina and Chile) and in the South Island of New Zealand.
    {Mushroom^0.5|Jack|Bun}^[((Base == "Black" || Base == "Chocolate" || Base == "BlackTort") && Agouti == "Tabby" && (Albino != "Normal" || White == "HighWhite" || White == "MidWhite")) && (NorthAm || SouthAm || Europe || British || SouthAf || WestAs || EastAs || Australia || NewZeal)]
      desc = Suillus luteus (slippery jack, sticky bun). Brown & dark grey mushroom with yellow pores and white stem. Native to Eurasia, it is widespread across the British Isles. To the east it has been recorded from Pakistan, where it was found along canals in Dashkin in the district of Astore, and as far east as South Korea. In North America it is found in the northeastern, northwestern, and southwestern United States. Places where it's introduced in include South America, Africa, Australia, and New Zealand. It has been recorded as far north as the Darling Downs and southern Queensland, and occasionally in Tasmania.
    {Mushroom^0.5|Suillus}^[((Base == "Red" || Base == "Cream" || Base == "Cinnamon" || Base == "CinnamonTort") && (Albino != "Normal" || White == "HighWhite" || White == "MidWhite")) && (Europe)]
