      desc = Suillus pungens (pungent slippery jack, pungent suillus). Grey mushroom with white stem. Found in California. Reportedly introduced within Australia and New Zealand.
    {Mushroom^0.5|Suillus}^[((Base == "FawnTort" || Base == "CinnamonTort") && Albino == "Normal" && (White == "NoWhite")) && (NorthAm || Islands)]
      desc = Suillus quiescens. Creamy brown mushroom with a yellow stem and pores. Found in Santa Cruz Island, Santa Rosa Island, and Point Reyes National Seashore in California.
    {Mushroom^0.5|Jill}^[((Base == "Cinnamon" || Base == "CinnamonTort") && Albino == "Normal" && (White == "NoWhite")) && (NorthAm || MidAm || SouthAf || EastAs || Japan || Australia || Hawaii || Islands)]
      desc = Suillus salmonicolor (Slippery Jill). Light brown mushroom. Found in North America, Kamchatka (in the Russian Far East), and in southern India. The northern limit of its North American range is eastern Canada (Quebec), and the southern limit is Nuevo León and near Nabogame in Temósachi Municipality, Chihuahua, Mexico. Has been collected from the Dominican Republic in the Caribbean, Japan, Taiwan, and from Mpumalanga, South Africa. Because there are no native Pinus species in South Africa, the fungus is assumed to be an exotic species that has been introduced via pine plantations. It has also been introduced to Australia, where it is known from a single collection in Queensland, and has been found growing in Belize. It is found in Hawaii.
    {Mushroom^0.5|Suillus}^[((Base == "Cinnamon" || Base == "CinnamonTort" || Base == "Red") && (Albino != "Normal" || White == "HighWhite" || White == "MidWhite")) && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Suillus serotinus. Light brown mushroom. Found in eastern North America.
    {Mushroom^0.5|Jack}^[((Base == "Cream") && Albino == "Normal" && (White == "NoWhite")) && (NorthAm || Europe || WestAs || EastAs)]
      desc = Suillus sibiricus (Siberian slippery jack). Pale yellow mushroom. It is found in mountains of Europe, North America, and Siberia.
