      desc = Suillus spraguei (painted slipperycap, painted suillus, red and yellow suillus). Red-brown and yellow mushroom. Has a disjunct distribution and is known from several localities in Asia, including China, Japan, Korea, and Taiwan. In North America, its range extends from eastern Canada (Nova Scotia) south to the Carolinas, and west to Minnesota. It has also been collected in Mexico (Coahuila and Durango). Furthermore, the species has been introduced to Europe (Germany, Lower Saxony; Netherlands).
    {Mushroom^0.5|Suillus}^[((Base == "Cream") && Albino == "Normal" && (White == "NoWhite")) && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Suillus subaureus. Pale mushroom with cream mottled cap. It is found in North America.
    {Mushroom^0.5|Suillus}^[((Base == "ChocolateTort" || Base == "CinnamonTort" || ((Base == "Chocolate" || Base == "Cinnamon") && Agouti == "Tabby")) && Albino == "Normal" && (White == "NoWhite")) && (NorthAm)]
