      desc = Clavariadelphus ligula (strap coral). Pale creamy mushroom growing as groups of stalks. The species has been collected in the Czech Republic, in Austria (data in), the Magadan region of the Russian Far East as well as the arctic zone of the Urals. It has also been collected in Kashmir Valley in India. In North America, the distribution extends north to Canada.
    {Mushroom^0.5|Coral}^[((Base == "Cream") && Albino == "Normal" && (White == "NoWhite")) && (NorthAm || Europe || British)]
