      desc = Ramaria rubrievanescens (fading pink coral). White coral fungus with pale pink-tipped branches. It is found in North America.
    {Mushroom^0.5|Coral}^[(Base == "White" || ((Base == "Pink") && (White == "HighWhite" || Albino != "Normal"))) && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Ramaria rubripermanens. White coral fungus with pinkish grey-tipped branches. Known from the western United States, including Washington, Idaho, and Oregon. It has also been recorded in Mexico.
    {Mushroom^0.5|Coral}^[(Base == "White" || Base == "Cream") && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Ramaria stricta (strict-branch coral, strict coral mushroom, upright coral). Pale creamy pink coral mushroom. Found in coniferous forests of the Pacific Coast and Rocky Mountains.
    {Mushroom^0.5|Coral}^[(Base == "White" || ((Base == "Pink") && (White == "HighWhite" || Albino != "Normal"))) && (NorthAm || Europe || WestAs)]
      desc = Ramaria subbotrytis. White coral fungus with pink-tipped branches. Described as appearing in Slovakia, the Czech Republic, the Urals of Russia, the Jilotzingo region of Mexico, throughout the Iberian Peninsula, and throughout the United States and Canada, making the species widely geographically distributed.
    {Mushroom^0.5|Coral}^[(((Base == "Cream" && Rufous == "High")) && (White == "HighWhite" || Albino != "Normal")) && (NorthAm)]
