    {Mushroom^0.5|Vase|Chanterelle}^[((Base == "Red") && (White == "HighWhite" || Albino != "Normal")) && (NorthAm || EastAs || Japan || Australia)]
      desc = Turbinellus floccosus (scaly vase or the shaggy-, scaly-, or woolly chanterelle). White mushroom with an orange bowl-shaped top. Occurs in North America, particularly the western states. It is most abundant in rainy parts of the Pacific Northwest, northern California and the Sierra Nevada. It also occurs across Asia, having been recorded from Japan, North Korea, China, Tibet, India, Nepal and Pakistan. Has been occasionally recorded from introduced conifer plantations in Australia.
    {Mushroom^0.5|Chanterelle}^[(((Base == "Red" && Rufous == "Low") || (Base == "Cream" && Rufous == "High")) && (White == "HighWhite" || Albino != "Normal")) && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Turbinellus kauffmanii (scaly vase false chanterelle). White mushroom with a golden spiky bowl-shaped top. Native to the Pacific Northwest and northern California. It has also been recorded from Amanalco municipality in central Mexico.
