    //Ileodictyon
    {Mushroom|Fungus}^[(Base == "White") && (Australia || NewZeal || SouthAm || British)]
      desc = Ileodictyon cibarium (basket fungus or the white basket fungus + about 35 Māori names). White web-shaped mushroom. Native to New Zealand and Australia and has also been introduced to Chile, Brazil, Africa and England.
    {Mushroom|Fungus}^[(Base == "White") && (Australia || EastAs || Japan || Europe || British)]
      desc = Ileodictyon gracile (smooth cage fungus). White web-shaped mushroom. Native to Australia, but is not known with certainty from New Zealand. The species has also been found in Asia, in China, India, Japan, and Korea, possibly as a result of it being introduced. It is also known in Europe from England, Italy, Portugal, and Spain where it is certainly introduced. 
    //Itajahya
    {Mushroom^0.5|Stinkhorn}^[((Base == "Black" || Base == "Blue" || Base == "Lilac") && (White == "HighWhite" || Albino == "Point")) && (Australia || NorthAm || SouthAf)]
      desc = Itajahya galericulata (jacaranda helmet stinkhorn). Black or grey stinkhorn mushroom with a white stalk. Found in Australia, North America (introduced), and South Africa (possibly introduced).
    //Laternea
    Mushroom^[((Base == "Red") && Albino == "Normal" && (White == "NoWhite")) && (MidAm || SouthAm)]
      desc = Laternea triscapa. Orange tendril-shapped mushroom. It is found in Central and South America, and the West Indies.
    //Ligiella
    Mushroom^[(Base == "White") && (MidAm)]
      desc = Ligiella rodrigueziana. White cage-shaped mushroom. Found in Costa Rica.
    //Lysurus
    {Mushroom^0.5|Stinkhorn}^[((Base == "Red") && (White == "HighWhite" || Albino == "Point")) && (NorthAm || SouthAf)]
      desc = Lysurus cruciatus (lizard's-claw stinkhorn). Pale cream mushroom with a split orange top. Found in North America and Africa.
    {Mushroom^0.5|Stinkhorn|Claw|Lizardclaw}^[(((Base == "Red" && Rufous == "High") || Base == "BlackTort") && (White != "MidWhite" || Albino != "Normal")) && (NorthAm || Europe || EastAs || Japan || Australia || NewZeal || Islands)]
      desc = Lysurus mokusin (lantern stinkhorn, small lizard's claw, ribbed lizard claw). Pale cream or pink spike-shaped mushroom. Documented sightings include Australasia, the Canary Islands, Korea, Japan, China (Fujian Province), and the Bonin Islands. In Europe, only reported from Italy. In the United States, it has been collected from the states of California, Texas, Northeast Oklahoma and Washington, D.C.
    {Mushroom^0.5|Stinkhorn}^[((Base == "Red") && (White == "HighWhite" || Albino == "Point")) && (NorthAm || MidAm || SouthAm || SouthAf || EastAs || SEastAs || Islands)]
      desc = Lysurus periphragmoides (stalked lattice stinkhorn, chambered stinkhorn). Pinkish mushroomm with small orange cap. Reported from Africa (Mauritius, Tanzania), Asia (Jilin Province, China, Sri Lanka, India, Pakistan, Thailand, Indonesia), New Guinea, Bahamas, Dominica, Mexico, Central America (Nicaragua) and South America (Argentina, Uruguay, Brazil, and Venezuela). The distribution extends north to the Ryukyu Islands in Asia. It is fairly common in South America.
    //Phallus
    {Mushroom^0.5|Stinkhorn}^[((Base == "Chocolate" || Base == "Cinnamon") && (White == "HighWhite" || Albino == "Point")) && (MidAm)]
      desc = Phallus atrovolvatus. White mushroom with a small round brown cap, and a webbed 'skirt'. Found in Costa Rica.
    {Mushroom^0.5|Stinkhorn}^[((Base == "BlackTort") && Albino == "Normal" && (White == "NoWhite")) && (NorthAf)]
      desc = Phallus aurantiacus. Yellow mushroom with a partially black cap. Found in Nigeria.
    {Mushroom^0.5|Stinkhorn}^[((Base == "BlackTort" || Base == "BlueTort" || Base == "ChocolateTort") && (White == "HighWhite" || Albino == "Point")) && (EastAs)]
      desc = Phallus cinnabarinus. White mushroom with a small round grey cap, and a cream webbed 'skirt'. Found in Taiwan.
    {Mushroom^0.5|Stinkhorn|Witch}^[((Base == "Black" && Agouti != "Agouti") && (White == "HighWhite" || White == "MidWhite")) && (NorthAm || SouthAm || EastAs || Japan)]
      desc = Phallus duplicatus (netted stinkhorn, wood witch). Black mushroom with a thick white base. Known from Asia (China and Japan), eastern North America, and South America (Brazil).
    {Mushroom^0.5|Stinkhorn}^[(Base == "White") && (SouthAm)]
      desc = Phallus granulosodenticulatus. White largely spike-shaped mushroom. Found in São Leopoldo, Brazil.
    {Mushroom^0.5|Stinkhorn}^[(((Base == "Black" || Base == "BlackTort") && Agouti != "Agouti") && (White == "HighWhite" || White == "MidWhite")) && (NorthAm || Europe || British || WestAs || EastAs || Japan || Australia)]
      desc = Phallus hadriani (dune stinkhorn, sand stinkhorn). Black mushroom with a white base. Known from North America, Europe (including Denmark, Ireland, Latvia, The Netherlands, Norway, Poland, Slovakia, Sweden, Ukraine, and Wales) Turkey (Iğdır Province), Japan, and China (Jilin Province). Also found in Australia, where it's assumed to be introduced.
    {Mushroom^0.5|Stinkhorn}^[((Base == "Black" || Base == "BlackTort") && (White == "HighWhite" || Albino == "Point")) && (EastAs)]
      desc = Phallus haitangensis. White mushroom with a black cap with orangish ridges, and a webbed 'skirt'. Found in Yunnan, China.
    {Mushroom^0.5|Stinkhorn}^[((Base == "Black" || Base == "Blue") && Agouti != "Solid" && (White == "HighWhite" || Albino == "Point")) && (NorthAm || MidAm || Europe || SouthAf || EastAs || Australia || Islands)]
      desc = Phallus impudicus (common stinkhorn). Mottled dark grey mushroom with a white stalk. Found throughout much of Europe and North America, and it has also been collected in Asia (including China, Taiwan, and India), Costa Rica, Iceland, Tanzania, and southeast Australia. In North America, it is most common west of the Mississippi River.
    {Mushroom^0.5|Stinkhorn|Pith|Veil|Lady}^[((Base == "Chocolate" || Base == "Blue") && (White == "HighWhite" || Albino == "Point")) && (NorthAm || MidAm || SouthAm || NorthAf || SouthAf || EastAs || Japan || SEastAs || Australia || Islands)]
      desc = Phallus indusiatus (basket stinkhorn, bamboo mushrooms, bamboo pith, long net stinkhorn, crinoline stinkhorn, bridal veil, veiled lady). Grey-brown mushroom with a white stalk and white webbed veil. Tropical, including Africa (Congo, Nigeria, Uganda, and Zaire), South America (Brazil Guyana, and Venezuela), Central America (Costa Rica), and Tobago. In North America, its range is restricted to Mexico. Asian localities include Indonesia, Nepal, Malaysia, India, Southern China, Japan, and Taiwan. It has also been collected in Australia.
    {Mushroom^0.5|Stinkhorn}^[((Base == "BlackTort" || (Base == "Black" && Agouti == "Tabby" && Gold != "None" && !Silver)) && (White == "NoWhite" && Albino == "Normal")) && (NorthAm || EastAs || Japan)]
      desc = Phallus luteus. Yellow-laced black mushroom with a yellow stalk and webbed veil. Widely distributed in Asia, including China, Korea, Japan, and India, and has been collected in Mexico.
    {Mushroom^0.5|Stinkhorn}^[(((Base == "BlackTort" || Base == "ChocolateTort" || ((Base == "Black" || Base == "Chocolate") && Agouti == "Tabby" && Gold != "None" && !Silver)) && Albino == "Normal") || (((Base == "Red" && Rufous == "Low") || (Base == "Cream" && Rufous == "High"))) && (White == "HighWhite" || Albino == "Point")) && (MidAm || SouthAf || SEastAs || Australia || Hawaii || Islands)]
      desc = Phallus multicolor. Yellow mushroom with a white stalk and laced veil. May also be brown with an orange veil. Found in Australia, Guam, Sumatra, Java, Borneo, Papua New Guinea, DRC, and Tobago as well as Hawaii and New Caledonia. 
    {Mushroom^0.5|Stinkhorn}^[((Base == "Lilac" || Base == "Blue") && (White == "HighWhite" || Albino == "Point")) && (NorthAm || MidAm)]
      desc = Phallus ravenelii (Ravenel's stinkhorn). Light grey mushroom with a white stalk. Widespread in eastern North America, from Quebec in the north, south to Florida and west to Iowa and Ohio. Also found in Costa Rica.
    {Mushroom^0.5|Stinkhorn}^[((Base == "BlackTort" || (Base == "Black" && Agouti == "Tabby" && Gold != "None" && !Silver)) && (White == "NoWhite" && Albino == "Normal")) && (NorthAm || MidAm || SouthAm || NorthAf || SouthAf || EastAs || Japan || SEastAs || Australia || Hawaii)]
      desc = Phallus rubicundus. Black mushroom with golden stalk. Widely distributed in southern and eastern United States (including Hawaii), having possibly been spread through the use of imported wood mulch in landscaping. In Australia it grows mainly in the tropics and subtropics. In Asia, it has been recorded from China, Japan, Korea, India, and Thailand. African locales include Ghana, Nigeria, Congo, Kenya, and South Africa. It is also known from South America (Argentina and Brazil) and the Caribbean.
    //Clathrus
    {Mushroom^0.5|Stinkhorn|{Devil's-fingers|Devilfinger}}^[((Base == "BlackTort" || (Base == "Black" && Agouti == "Tabby" && !Silver)) && (White == "NoWhite" || White == "LowWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || Europe || British || SouthAf || Australia || NewZeal)]
      desc = Clathrus archeri (octopus stinkhorn, devil's fingers). Red-pink mushroom growing in black-splotched tentacle shapes from a white base. Believed to be endemic to southern Africa, New Zealand and Australia, but has been spreading to other continents and is often invasive. Has been naturalised in Europe and North America.
    //Pseudocolus
    {Mushroom^0.5|Stinkhorn|Squid}^[((Base == "BlackTort" || Base == "Black") && Agouti == "Tabby" && Tabby == "Spotted" && !Silver && (White == "NoWhite" || White == "LowWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || Europe || WestAs || Japan || SEastAs || Australia || Hawaii || Islands)]
      desc = Pseudocolus fusiformis (stinky squid). Red-pink mushroom growing in black-splotched tentacle shapes from a white base. Collected from a variety of locations worldwide, including Europe, Australia, Japan, Java, the Philippines, Reunion Island, the United States, and Turkey. It is thought to have been introduced from southeast Asia to North America. In the continental United States, it has been found in Alabama, Connecticut, Georgia, Louisiana, Florida, Massachusetts, Mississippi, New Jersey, New York, North Carolina, Rhode Island, Tennessee, and Virginia; it has also been found in Hawaii.
    //Staheliomyces
    {Mushroom^0.5|Stinkhorn}^[((Base == "Black" && White == "HighWhite") || Base == "White") && (NorthAm || MidAm || SouthAm)]
      desc = Staheliomyces cinctus. White laced mushroom with a dark grey area connecting two sections. It is distributed from southern Mexico to southern Brazil.


    //AURICULARIALES
    
      

      
    
    //Acanthotrema
    Lichen^[((Base == "Lilac") && (White == "NoWhite" || White == "LowWhite") && (Albino == "Normal" || Albino == "Sepia")) && (MidAm)]
      desc = Acanthotrema alboisidiatum. A light olive-green lichen that grows in small patches on wood, and is distinguished by small white offshoots resembling insect eggs. Found in Puerto Rico.
    //Acarospora
    Lichen^[(((Base == "Red" && Rufous == "Low") || (Base == "Cream" && Rufous == "High")) && White == "NoWhite" && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || EastAs)]
      desc = Acarospora contigua (gold cobblestone lichen). A yellow-green lichen growing on stone, found in North America and the Eastern Ghats India.
    Lichen^[((Base == "BlackTort" || (Agouti == "Tabby" && Base == "Black") || Base == "Chocolate" || Base == "Cinnamon" || Base == "ChocolateTort" || Base == "CinnamonTort" || Base == "Red") && White == "NoWhite" && Albino != "Point") && (NorthAm || Europe || British)]
      desc = Acarospora fuscata (brown cobblestone lichen). A pale or yellow-ish brown lichen growing on stone. It grows in Europe and North America.
    Lichen^[((Base == "BlackTort" || (Agouti == "Tabby" && Base == "Black")) && White == "NoWhite" && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Acarospora obnubila (cloudy cobblestone lichen). A dull brown lichen growing on stone. They are common in Arizona, southern California, and Baja California.
    Lichen^[(((Base == "Red" && Rufous == "Low") || (Base == "Cream" && Rufous == "High") || (Gold != "Normal" && !Silver && Agouti == "Tabby")) && White == "NoWhite" && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Acarospora schleicheri. A yellow-green lichen growing on soil, found in arid habitats of southern California and Baja California.
    Lichen^[(((Base == "Red" && Rufous == "Low") || (Base == "Cream" && Rufous == "High") || (Gold != "Normal" && !Silver && Agouti == "Tabby")) && White == "NoWhite" && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Acarospora socialis (bright cobblestone lichen). A yellow-green lichen, found mostly on rock in western North America.
    Lichen^[(Base == "White" || (Silver && Gold == "Wideband" && Agouti == "Tabby")) && (NorthAm || SouthAm || Europe || British || NorthAf || SouthAf || WestAs || EastAs || Islands)]
      desc = Acarospora strigata. A lichen that is naturally brown, but typically appears pale grey. Grows on rock across the world.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Chocolate" || Base == "Cinnamon") && White == "NoWhite" && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || WestAs || Islands)]
      desc = Acarospora thamnina. A brown lichen growing along cracks in boulders. It can be found in North America to Alaska and Maine , from the coast to inland locations, also in the Ural Mountains and Novaya Zemlya in Russia.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Black" || Base == "Chocolate") && (White == "HighWhite" || Albino == "Point" || (Agouti != "Solid" && Silver && Tabby == "Spotted"))) && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Acarospora thelococcoides (soil eyes lichen). A lichen that grows as a white ring over a dark brown disc, making it appear like a collection of eyes. It grows from San Benito, California to Baja California.
    //Acroscyphus
    Lichen^[(Base == "White" || (((Base == "Red" && Rufous == "Low") || (Base == "Cream" && Rufous == "High") || Base == "BlackTort" || (!Silver && Agouti == "Tabby" && Gold != "None")))) && (NorthAm || SouthAm || SouthAf || EastAs || Japan)]
      desc = Acroscyphus sphaerophoroides. A white or yellow lichen growing as black-tipped branches. Found in western North America, including Mexico and British Columbia, as well as high exposed regions of Asia (China, Japan), South Africa, Peru, and Patagonia.
    //Agonimia
    Lichen^[(Base == "Green" && White == "NoWhite" && Albino == "Normal" && !Silver && Gold == "None" && Rufous != "High") && (NorthAm || Europe || British)]
      desc = Agonimia octospora. A green lichen growing on bark in Europe and North America.
    //Ahtiana
    Lichen^[(Base == "White" || Base == "Cream") && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Ahtiana sphaerosporella (mountain candlewax lichen). A pale cream lichen found in western North America.
    //Alectoria
    Lichen^[(Base == "White") && (NorthAm || Europe)]
      desc = Alectoria sarmentosa (common witch's-hair lichen). Pale green lichen growing as long tendrils. Found in Pacific Northwest Coast forests, including Alaska, Coastal British Columbia, Oregon, Washington, and northern California, west of Alberta and Montana. It also has been identified in the Appalachian Mountains temperate rainforest of Eastern U.S. and Boreal rainforests of New Brunswick and Nova Scotia Canada, as well as Scandinavian coastal conifer forests.
    //Amandinea
    Lichen^[((Base == "Black") && (Agouti != "Solid") && White == "NoWhite" && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Amandinea milliaria. A lichen growing on bark as a green patch with black bumps. Found in the east coast of North America, ranging from Prince Edward Island south to Texas, and includes the Great Lakes region.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Black") && (Agouti != "Solid") && White == "NoWhite" && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Amandinea punctata (tiny button lichen). A lichen growing on bark as a pale grey patch with black bumps. Found in California.
    //Anaptychia
    {Lichen|Eaglesclaws}^[(((Base == "Black") && (Agouti != "Solid") && !Silver && Gold == "None" && White == "NoWhite" && Albino == "Normal") || Base == "White") && (Europe || British || NorthAf || WestAs || EastAs || Islands)]
      desc = Anaptychia ciliaris (great ciliated lichen, eagle's claws). A green shrub-like lichen primarily found in Northern Europe, extending eastward to European Russia, the Caucasus, and northeastern Russia (Murmansk). It is also present in Central and Southern Europe, and the Canary Islands. In Africa, it is established across Morocco, and has been reported from Sudan. In China, specimens have been collected from Xinjiang, Gansu, Shaanxi, and Hebei. Among the top three most abundant lichens in Turkey's Lake Abant Nature Park.
    Lichen^[((Base == "FawnTort" || Base == "CinnamonTort" || (Albino != "Normal" && (Base == "Cinnamon" || Base == "Chocolate" || Base == "ChocolateTort"))) && (White == "NoWhite" || White == "LowWhite")) && (NorthAm || Europe || British)]
      desc = Anaptychia runcinata. A lichen growing on rocks at sea level. It's light brown and cream, found in Europe and North America.
    //Anzia
    Lichen^[((((Base == "Black" && (Agouti != "Solid")) || Base == "Lilac") && !Silver && Gold == "None" && White == "NoWhite" && Albino == "Normal") || Base == "White") && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Anzia colpodes (black foam lichen). A green to grey lichen growing on trees in North America.
    //Arthonia
    Lichen^[((Base == "Black") && (Agouti == "Solid") && White == "NoWhite" && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || Europe || British || WestAs || EastAs || Islands)]
      desc = Arthonia vinosa. A lichen growing on wood as small black spots(?). Found primarily in Europe.
    // /Aspicilia
    Lichen^[(Base == "White" || (Silver && Agouti == "Tabby" && Gold == "Wideband")) && (NorthAm || Europe || British || WestAs || EastAs || SEastAs || Japan)]
      desc = Aspicilia cinerea (cinder lichen). A pale, almost white lichen growing as a patch on rock in Eurasia, and North America.
    Lichen^[(Base == "Blue" && White == "NoWhite" && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Aspicilia confusa. A grey lichen growing on rock in California.
    Lichen^[(Base == "Cream" && White == "NoWhite" && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Aspicilia cuprea (copper sunken disk lichen). A cream lichen growing on rock in northern California to Baja California.
    Lichen^[(Base == "White" || (Silver && Agouti == "Tabby" && Gold == "Wideband")) && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Aspicilia cyanescens (bluish sunken disk lichen). A pale grey lichen growing as a patch on rock. Endemic to California.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Lilac" || Base == "LilacTort") && White == "NoWhite" && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Aspicilia pacifica (pacific sunken disk lichen). A pale grey lichen growing on rock in higher coastal mountains of California and Baja California.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Blue" || Base == "BlueTort") && White == "NoWhite" && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Aspicilia phaea (dusky sunken disk lichen). A grey lichen growing on rock in coastal to inland parts of central and southern California.
    //Astrothelium
    Lichen^[(((Base == "Red" && Rufous == "Low") || (Base == "Cream" && Rufous == "High") || (Gold != "Normal" && !Silver && Agouti == "Tabby")) && White == "NoWhite" && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || MidAm || SouthAm || SEastAs || Australia || NewZeal || Islands)]
      desc = Astrothelium aeneum. A yellow lichen growing on bark in tropical regions globally. Its presence has been recorded in various countries including the United States, Costa Rica, El Salvador, the Revillagigedo Islands, the Bahamas, Cuba, Jamaica, Colombia, Venezuela, Guyana, Suriname, French Guiana, the Galápagos Islands, Bolivia, Brazil, Sri Lanka, Thailand, and Malaysia (specifically in Sarawak and Sabah). Additionally, it is found in Papua New Guinea and Australia.
    //Athallia
    Lichen^[(((Base == "Red" && Rufous == "Low") || (Base == "Cream" && Rufous == "High") || (Gold != "Normal" && !Silver && Agouti == "Tabby")) && White == "NoWhite" && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || Europe || Islands)]
      desc = Athallia scopularis. A golden lichen growing on rock from Atlantic coasts of North America, Northern Europe, and Greenland.
    //Atla
    Lichen^[((Base == "Black" && (Agouti != "Tabby" || (Silver && Tabby == "Spotted")))) && (Europe || Islands)]
      desc = Atla alpina. A lichen growing on rocks, it's characterised by black 'lumps'. In addition to Sweden, the lichen has been recorded from Scandinavia, Spitsbergen, Novaya Zemlya, Austria, and Germany.
    //Baeomyces
    Lichen^[((Silver && Gold == "Wideband" && Agouti != "Solid")) && (NorthAm || MidAm || Europe || NewZeal || Hawaii)]
      desc = Baeomyces carneus. A pale green crust lichen growing on soil or rock, it grows tiny brown mushrooms(?). It is widely distributed in the boreal forest region of North America, and also occurs in Europe, New Zealand, the West Indies, and Hawaii. 
    Lichen^[((Base == "Lilac" || Base == "Fawn")) && (Australia || NewZeal || Islands)]
      desc = Baeomyces heteromorphus. A ground-dwelling green lichen with grey fruiting bodies. The species is commonly found across mainland Australia and New Zealand. Also occurs in New Guinea, and Fiji. It has also been recorded from Kaikōura Island. It also extends its habitat to the subantarctic region, with documented populations on Macquarie Island.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Black" || Base == "BlackTort") && Agouti == "Tabby" && White == "NoWhite" && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || Europe || WestAs || EastAs)]
      desc = Baeomyces rufus (brown beret lichen). A green lichen with pinkish brown fruiting bodies. It is found in circumpolar North America, Asia, and Europe.
    //Bagliettoa
    Lichen^[((Base == "Pink") && White == "NoWhite" && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || Europe || British)]
      desc = Bagliettoa marmorea. A pink lichen growing on rock. Widespread in Europe. Also recorded from North America, but this could be a different species.
    //Bathelium
    Lichen^[((Base == "Black" || Base == "Chocolate" || Base == "Cinnamon") && (Agouti == "Tabby" && Tabby == "Spotted") && (White == "NoWhite" && Albino == "Normal")) && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Bathelium carolinianum. A greenish brown lichen with darker brown 'warts'. It grows on wood in the eastern United States.
    //Bellemerea
    Lichen^[((Base == "Lilac") && (White == "NoWhite" && Albino == "Normal")) && (NorthAm || Europe || WestAs || EastAs || Australia || NewZeal || Islands)]
      desc = Bellemerea alpina (brown sunken disk lichen). A pale grey lichen growing on rocks. It grows in arctic-alpine habitats in Eurasia, North America (south to California and Arizona), Australia, and New Zealand.
    //Biatora
    Lichen^[(Base == "Green" && (White == "NoWhite" && Albino == "Normal")) && (MidAm || SouthAm || SouthAf || SEastAs)]
      desc = Biatora kalbii. A green lichen found in pantropic regions. 
    Lichen^[(Base == "Green" && (White == "NoWhite" && Albino == "Normal")) && (NorthAm || Europe || NorthAf || SouthAf || WestAs || Japan)]
      desc = Biatora pontica. A green lichen found on bark. It is widely distributed in Europe, having been recorded in Austria, Italy, Norway, Poland, Russia, and Slovenia. It also occurs in Africa, Asia, and North America. 
    Lichen^[(Base == "Cinnamon" || Base == "Red" || Base == "BlackTort" || Base == "ChocolateTort" || Base == "CinnamonTort") && (NorthAm || MidAm || Europe || British || WestAs || EastAs || Japan || Islands)]
      desc = Biatora vernalis. A lichen notable for small orange fruiting bodies. Found across Eurasia and North America.
    //Blastenia
    Lichen^[(Base == "Cinnamon" || Base == "CinnamonTort") && (Europe || British || NorthAf || SouthAf)]
      desc = Blastenia ferruginea. A lichen growing on bark notable for small orange-brown fruiting bodies. In the United Kingdom, it is scarce and appears to be declining, with recent records mostly from Northern and Western Scotland, Western Ireland, and sporadically in Cumbria, Hampshire, and Sussex. It has become rare or extinct in most parts of England, Wales, and Central Europe. Rrecorded as new to tropical Africa, and had previously been reported from South Africa and Morocco.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Lilac" || Base == "Fawn" || (Silver && Tabby == "Agouti" && Gold == "Wideband"))) && (NorthAm || Europe || WestAs || Islands)]
      desc = Brodoa intestiniformis. A pale grey lichen found in arctic and boreal regions.
    //Bryoria
    {Lichen^2|Moss}^[(Base == "Red" && White == "NoWhite" && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || Europe || WestAs || EastAs)]
      desc = Bryoria fremontii (black moss, black tree lichen, edible horsehair lichen). A golden-brown lichen hanging from trees. Common in western North America, being found throughout most of the interior of British Columbia, extending east into the Alberta Rockies, and south into Montana, Idaho, and Wyoming, as well as being found in Washington, Oregon, and California. It also grows in Europe and Russia.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Lilac") && (White == "NoWhite" && Albino == "Normal")) && (NorthAm || Europe || British || SouthAf || WestAs || EastAs || Japan || Hawaii || Islands)]
      desc = Bryoria fuscescens. A pale grey lichen growing on trees. Found across the world(?).
    Lichen^[((Base == "Fawn" || Base == "Cream" || Base == "FawnTort") && (White == "NoWhite" && Albino == "Normal")) && (NorthAm || Europe || Islands)]
      desc = Bryoria pseudofuscescens. A creamy grey lichen growing on trees. Found in North America, Europe, Iceland(?).
    //Buellia
    Lichen^[((Base == "Black") && (Silver && Agouti == "Tabby" && Tabby == "Spotted")) && (NorthAm || Europe)]
      desc = Buellia aethalea (darkened button lichen). A pale lichen with black spots growing in temperate areas. Particularly common in Northern Europe.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Black" || Base == "Chocolate") && Agouti != "Tabby" && (White == "NoWhite" && Albino == "Normal")) && (NorthAm || Europe || NorthAf)]
      desc = Buellia badia (parasitic button lichen). A dark brown lichen that parasitises other lichens. It's found in Europe, northern Africa, and North America.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Black") && (Silver && Agouti == "Tabby" && Tabby == "Spotted")) && (NorthAm || Europe || NorthAf)]
      desc = Buellia dispersa. A pale grey lichen with small black spots that grows on rock. Found in northern Africa, Europe, and southwestern North America.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Black") && (Silver && Agouti == "Tabby" && Tabby == "Spotted")) && (NorthAm || Europe)]
      desc = Buellia erubescens (common button lichen). A warm pale grey lichen with small black spots that grows on bark. Found throughout North America and Europe.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Blue" || Base == "Black") && (White == "NoWhite" && Albino == "Normal")) && (Antarctica)]
      desc = Buellia frigida. A grey (mix of black and white, which appears grey) lichen growing on rock. Endemic to maritime and continental Antarctica.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Lilac" || Base == "Fawn" || (Silver && Golden == "Wideband" && Agouti == "Tabby"))) && (NorthAm || Europe || NorthAf || WestAs || NewZeal)]
      desc = Buellia griseovirens. Pale green-grey lichen growing on bark. Distributed in Europe, Mediterranean Africa, the Middle East, and North America, including montane areas of southern California (Riverside and Los Angeles Counties). In Canada, it is found in Alberta, British Columbia, Nova Scotia, Ontario, and the Yukon Territory. In the United States, it occurs in Montana and Wyoming. It is also found in New Zealand.
