    Lichen^[(((Base == "Red" && Rufous == "Low") || (Base == "Cream" && Rufous == "High")) && White == "NoWhite" && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || Europe || British)]
      desc = Candelaria concolor (candleflame lichen, lemon lichen). A greenish yellow lichen. Very common species in North America and Europe.
    Lichen^[(((Base == "Red" && Rufous == "Low") || (Base == "Cream" && Rufous == "High")) && White == "NoWhite" && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || MidAm || SouthAm || Europe || WestAs)]
      desc = Candelaria pacifica. A greenish yellow lichen growing on bark. his species was first identified on the western coast of North America, where its range extends from the Sonoran Desert in the United States all the way up to the states of Washington and Idaho, stretching into Canada and South America. Its European distribution includes France, Belgium, Luxembourg, Poland, Estonia, Switzerland, Russia, Germany, the Netherlands, and Scandinavian counties. It has also been found in Iran.
    //Candelariella
