      desc = Candelariella aggregata. A yellow lichen growing on moss or plant debri. Originally found in the Rocky Mountains and the Cascade Range. Since then also discovered in Switzerland and Mongolia.
    Lichen^[(Base == "White") && (NorthAm || SouthAm || Europe || WestAs || EastAs || Australia)]
      desc = Candelariella antennaria (pussytoes eggyolk lichen). A tiny white lichen found on bark. Distributed in North America, and has been observed in South America, Asia, Australia, and Europe.
    {Lichen|Eggyolk|Goldspeck}^[(((Base == "Red" && Rufous == "Low") || (Base == "Cream" && Rufous == "High"))) && (NorthAm || Europe)]
      desc = Candelariella aurella (hidden goldspeck lichen, eggyolk lichen). A scattered yellow lichen growing on limestone and sandstone. Found in the Sonoran Desert in Arizona, California, and Baja California. Also known in Europe.
    {Lichen|Goldfleck}^[(((Base == "Red" && Rufous == "Low") || (Base == "Cream" && Rufous == "High")) && White == "NoWhite" && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Candelariella efflorescens (powdery goldfleck lichen). A golden lichen growing on bark and wood in temperate eastern North American distribution. 
    Lichen^[(Base == "Green" && White == "NoWhite" && Albino == "Normal") && (Europe || WestAs)]
