      desc = Chrysothrix candelaris (mustard powder lichen, gold dust lichen). A bright yellow lichen typically found on trees. It is found in the United Kingdom, North America, Scotland, Hungary, Iran, Latvia and has been recorded in the Cape Verde Islands.
    Lichen^[(Base == "Green" && White == "NoWhite" && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Chrysothrix chamaecyparicola. Pale green lichen dusting bark. The species is most prevalent in the mid-Atlantic region of the United States, namely in New Jersey, Maryland, and Pennsylvania.
    Lichen^[(((Gold != "None" && !Silver && Agouti == "Tabby") || (Base == "Red" && Rufous == "Low") || (Base == "Cream" && Rufous == "High")) && White == "NoWhite" && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || Europe || WestAs || EastAs || SEastAs || Islands || Antarctica)]
      desc = Chrysothrix chlorina (sulphur dust lichen). Yellow-green lichen typically found on rock. It predominantly thrives within the boreal forest zones of Europe, spanning from northern Italy to Scandinavia. Its presence is also noted in the Himalayas and North America. In eastern North America, it has a northerly distribution, with documented collections reaching as far north as Lake Nipigon, Ontario, and Vermont. Additional records indicate occurrences in Macaronesia, Antarctica, the Russian Arctic, and the Tehri Garhwal district of Uttar Pradesh, India.
    Lichen^[(((Gold != "None" && !Silver && Agouti == "Tabby") || (Base == "Red" && Rufous == "Low") || (Base == "Cream" && Rufous == "High")) && White == "NoWhite" && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || Europe || Japan)]
      desc = Chrysothrix flavovirens. Yellow-green lichen typically found on bark. Widespread in Europe, and has also been recorded from Japan and North America.
