      desc = Chrysothrix insulizans. Yellow lichen typically found on rock. It is most prevalent in the southeastern United States and the Ozarks region.
    Lichen^[(((Gold != "None" && !Silver && Agouti == "Tabby") || (Base == "Red" && Rufous == "Low") || (Base == "Cream" && Rufous == "High")) && White == "NoWhite" && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || SouthAm || NorthAf || SouthAf || WestAs || EastAs || Islands || Australia || NewZeal)]
      desc = Chrysothrix xanthina. Yellow-green lichen typically found on bark. It has been recorded from Africa (including Madagascar), Asia, Macaronesia, New South Wales, North America, and South America. Chrysothrix xanthina is widespread in eastern North America, where its range extends west to the eastern edge of the mixed grass prairie ecotone found in the Great Plains. In 2007, it was reported for the first time from Tasmania, Norfolk Island, and New Zealand.
    //Circinaria
