      desc = Cladonia amaurocraea (quill lichen, quill cup lichen). Pale green shrub-like lichen. In North America, it is widespread throughout Canada and Alaska.
    {Lichen|Cladoniais}^[(Base == "Green" && White == "NoWhite" && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Cladonia apodocarpa (stalkless cladoniais, stalkless cup lichen). Bright green leafy lichen. Found in North America.
    Lichen^[(Base == "Green" && White == "NoWhite" && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || SouthAm || Europe || Antarctica)]
      desc = Cladonia asahinae (pixie cup lichen, Asahina's cup lichen). Bright green lichen growing as stalks. Found in Europe, North America, southern South America, and the Antarctic.
    Lichen^[((Base == "LilacTort" || Base == "BlueTort") || (Silver && Agouti == "Tabby" && (Base == "BlackTort" || Base == "ChocolateTort" || Base == "CinnamonTort"))) && (NorthAm || SouthAm || Europe || British || WestAs || EastAs || Islands || Antarctica)]
      desc = Cladonia borealis (boreal cup lichen). Grey-green lichen with bright red growths. It occurs in North and South America, Antarctica, Eurasia and many on islands.
    {Lichen|Cladonia}^[(Base == "White" || (Silver && Gold == "Wideband" && Agouti == "Tabby")) && (NorthAm || Japan)]
      desc = Cladonia boryi (fishnet cladonia, fishnet lichen, Bory's cup lichen). Pale silvery grey lichen found on soil. Mostly reported from the North East United States, occasionally reported elsewhere such as Japan.
    {Lichen|Cladonia}^[(Base == "Green" && White == "NoWhite" && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Cladonia caespiticia (stubby-stalked Cladonia). Leafy green lichen found in North America.
    {Lichen|Soldier{s|}}^[(White == "HighWhite" && Base == "Black") && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Cladonia cariosa (split-peg lichen, split-peg soldiers). A white and black spotted lichen. Widely distributed in North America.
