      desc = Dimelaena oreina (golden moonglow lichen). Yellow-green lichen with a dark grey center. Grows on rock. It is common in the Sonoran Desert of Arizona, California, Baja California, Baja California Sur, Sonora, Mexico, and Chihuahua, Mexico. Maybe has a worldwide distribution outside the tropics, Australasia, and Antarctica (though that's based on GBIF data from what I can tell).
    Lichen^[((Base == "Black" || Base == "Chocolate") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Dimelaena thysanota (mountain lichen). Dark grey-brown lichen found in the mountains of western North America and the Sonoran Desert.
    //Diorygma
    Lichen^[((Base == "Green") && (White == "NoWhite" || White == "LowWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (MidAm || SouthAm)]
      desc = Diorygma antillarum. White-rimmed green lichen growing on bark. Common and widespread in the Neotropical realm.
    //Diploicia
    Lichen^[(((Base == "Red" && Rufous == "Low") || (Base == "Cream" && Rufous == "High") || (Gold != "Normal" && !Silver && Agouti == "Tabby")) && (White == "HighWhite" || Albino != "Normal")) && (NorthAm || MidAm || SouthAm || Europe || NorthAf || SouthAf || WestAs || EastAs || SEastAs || Australia)]
      desc = Diploicia canescens. White and gold lichen. Found on every continent except Antarctica.
    //Diploschistes
    Lichen^[((Base == "Black" && Agouti == "Tabby" && Silver) && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || MidAm || SouthAm || Europe || British || SouthAf || WestAs || EastAs || SEastAs || Australia || NewZeal || Islands)]
      desc = Diploschistes scruposus (crater lichen). Pale grey to white lichen with black pits. Widespread.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Black" && ((Agouti == "Tabby" && Silver && Tabby == "Spotted") || White == "HighWhite")) && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || Europe || British || Australia || NewZeal || Islands)]
      desc = Diplotomma alboatrum. White lichen with black spots. Recorded in Europe, North America, and Australasia.
    //Dirina
    Lichen^[(Base == "White") && (Europe || NorthAf || WestAs || Islands)]
      desc = Dirina ceratoniae. White lichen growing on calcium-rich rock and bark. The lichen is common in Mediterranean Europe, with a range extending west to southern Portugal and northern Morocco. Found in Russia, in Dagestan. A couple of collections have been made in the Canary Islands, but it is thought that these are the result of introductions.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Lilac" || Base == "Blue") && (White == "HighWhite" || Albino != "Normal")) && (Europe || British || NorthAf)]
      desc = Dirina fallax. White lichen with light grey edges growing on rock. It is found in the western Mediterranean, the Atlantic coasts of both Africa and Europe (extending from Scotland to Morocco), and central Europe. Also reported from the Abrau Peninsula in Russia.
    //Dirinaria
    Lichen^[(((Base == "Red" && Rufous == "Low") || (Base == "Cream" && Rufous == "High") || Base == "LilacTort" || Base == "FawnTort") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || MidAm || SouthAm || SouthAf || EastAs || SEastAs || Australia)]
      desc = Dirinaria aegialita. Pale yellow-green lichen. Its distribution encompasses all tropical regions of both hemispheres, with occasional sightings in the eastern regions of subtropical North America. Particularly prominent within the Sonoran region, and sporadically within Baja California, Baja California Sur, Chihuahua, Sinaloa, and Sonora.
    Lichen^[(Base == "White") && (NorthAm || MidAm || SouthAm || Europe || NorthAf || SouthAf || WestAs || EastAs || SEastAs || Australia)]
      desc = Dirinaria applanata. Pale off-white lichen growing on bark. It has a wide distribution in tropical and subtropical areas of the world. 
    Lichen^[((Base == "Green" || (Base == "Black" && Agouti == "Tabby" && Tabby == "Spotted" && !Silver && Gold == "None")) && (White == "HighWhite" || White == "MidWhite" || Albino != "Normal")) && (NorthAm || MidAm || SouthAm || SouthAf || EastAs || Japan || SEastAs || Australia)]
      desc = Dirinaria confluens. Green & white lichen with black spots. The species is distributed across all tropical regions of both hemispheres, with occasional collections noted from subtropical areas of Japan. Predominantly found in Baja California, Baja California Sur, Sinaloa, and Sonora.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Green" || (Base == "Black" && Agouti == "Tabby" && Tabby == "Spotted" && !Silver && Gold == "None")) && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || MidAm || SouthAm)]
      desc = Dirinaria confusa. Pale green lichen with black spots found on bark or wood. Its distribution spans tropical and subtropical areas of North, Central, and South America, with notable occurrences in Texas.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Green") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (EastAs || NewZeal || Islands)]
      desc = Dirinaria picta. Green lichen growing on bark. Distributed in various locations, including the Kermadec Islands, Bangladesh, and several regions in New Zealand.
    //Dolichousnea
    {Lichen|Beard}^[(Base == "White") && (NorthAm || Europe || WestAs || EastAs)]
      desc = Dolichousnea longissima (old man's beard, Methuselah's beard lichen). Lichen growing as long white strands on trees. The longest lichen. Has medicinal uses. Found in Europe, Asia, and North America. In North America, it is primarily found on the Pacific Coast, and the largest populations are concentrated in the Pacific Northwest. It ranges from Upper Midwest into Canada, the Great Lakes region, and extends to the coast of the Atlantic ocean.
    //Dufourea
    Lichen^[(((Base == "Red" && Rufous == "Low") || (Base == "Cream" && Rufous == "High")) && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (Australia || NewZeal)]
      desc = Dufourea ligulata. Bright golden lichen growing on coastal rocks in Australasia. 
    //Dyplolabia
    Lichen^[((Base == "Red" || Base == "Green") && (White == "LowWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || MidAm || SouthAm || EastAs || SEastAs || Australia)]
      desc = Dyplolabia afzelii. Orange or olive green lichen with white ridges growing on bark. Found in Australia, Mexico, South America, the Caribbean, India, Thailand, and the Mid-Atlantic Coastal Plain of North Carolina in eastern North America.
    
    //Enchylium
    Lichen^[((Base == "Black" && Agouti != "Tabby") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || Europe || British || Islands)]
      desc = Enchylium limosum (lime-loving tarpaper lichen). Black lichen. Within Europe, the species has been recorded from a number of countries, including Italy, the United Kingdom, Ireland, the Czech Republic, Austria, Switzerland, and France. Outside of Europe, has been recorded in the Canadian provinces of British Columbia, Manitoba, Nova Scotia, Northwest Territories, Nunavut, Ontario, Prince Edward Island, and Quebec, as well as the U.S. state of Minnesota.
    //Enterographa
    Lichen^[(((Base == "Red" && Rufous == "Low") || (Base == "Cream" && Rufous == "High")) && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (Australia || NewZeal)]
      desc = Enterographa bella. Golden lichen growing as spots on leaves. Recorded from New Zealand, Victoria (Australia), and Tasmania.
    Lichen^[(Base == "White") && (SEastAs || Islands)]
      desc = Enterographa kinabaluensis. Pale silvery grey lichen growing on bark. Known only from its type locality in a coastal rainforest on Sapi Island, near Kota Kinabalu, Sabah, Malaysia.
    //Ephebe
    Lichen^[((Base == "Black" && Agouti != "Tabby") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Ephebe lanata (rockshag lichen). Black lichen. Found in North America.
    //Erioderma
    Lichen^[(((Base == "BlackTort" && Agouti == "Tabby") || Base == "Green") && (White != "HighWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || Europe || EastAs)]
      desc = Erioderma pedicellatum (boreal felt lichen). Leaf green lichen with a white underside and reddish or purplish spots. It grows on trees in damp boreal forests along the Atlantic coast in Canada, as well as in southcentral Alaska, the Kamchatka Peninsula, and Norway. Endangered.
    //Esslingeriana
    Lichen^[(((Base == "Green") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") || Base == "White") && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Esslingeriana idahoensis (tinted rag lichen). Pale grey-green leafy lichen. It is found in northwestern North America. 
    //Evernia
    Lichen^[(((Base == "Green") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") || Base == "White") && (NorthAm || Europe || WestAs || EastAs)]
      desc = Evernia divaricata. Pale yellowish-green branching lichen. It can be found in western North America, Europe, the Near East, and China.
    Lichen^[(((Base == "Green") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") || Base == "White") && (NorthAm || Europe || WestAs || EastAs || Japan)]
      desc = Evernia esorediosa. Pale green shrub-like lichen. It can be found in Japan, Russia, the United States of America, Canada and Mongolia.
    {Lichen^0.5|Oakmoss}^[(((Base == "Green") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") || Base == "White") && (NorthAm || Europe || British || NorthAf || WestAs || EastAs || Japan || Islands)]
      desc = Evernia prunastri (oakmoss). Pale green shrub-like lichen. It can be found in many mountainous temperate forests throughout the Northern Hemisphere.
    
    //Felipes
    Lichen^[((Base == "Black" && ((Agouti == "Tabby" && Silver) || White == "HighWhite")) && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || Europe || British)]
      desc = Felipes leucopellaeus. Whitish lichen with black speckling. Found across Europe and North America in temperate and boreal regions.
    //Fissurina
    Lichen^[(Base == "White") && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Fissurina alligatorensis. Smooth white-ish lichen growing on bark. Found throughout the Mid-Atlantic Coastal Plain and Southeastern Coastal Plain, from northeastern North Carolina to northern Florida.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Green") && (White != "HighWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || MidAm || SouthAm || SEastAs || Australia || NewZeal || Islands)]
      desc = Fissurina dumastii. Green or green & white lichen growing on trees. Considered pantropical.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Green" || Base == "Lilac")) && (MidAm || EastAs || Australia || NewZeal || Islands)]
      desc = Fissurina insidiosa. Grey-green lichen. Broad distribution in the Southern Hemisphere, with recorded presences in mainland Australia, New Zealand, the Pacific region, the Caribbean, and India.
    //Flavoparmelia
    Lichen^[((Base == "Green")) && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Flavoparmelia baltimorensis (rock greenshield lichen). Pale green leafy lichen growing on rock. Found in the United States and Canada.
    //Flavoplaca
    Lichen^[(((Base == "Red" && Rufous == "Low") || (Base == "Cream" && Rufous == "High")) && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (Europe || Islands)]
      desc = Flavoplaca arcis. Yellow lichen growing on rock. Its distribution spans Western and Central Europe, Scandinavia, the Mediterranean region, the Balkan Peninsula, and the Canary Islands.
    Lichen^[(((Base == "Red" && Rufous == "Low") || (Base == "Cream" && Rufous == "High")) && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (SouthAm || Europe)]
      desc = Flavoplaca austrocitrina. Yellow lichen growing on rock. Identified in various European countries, including Austria, Bulgaria, Germany, Greece, the Czech Republic, Romania, Russia, and Slovakia. Also found in the Buenos Aires region of Argentina. 
    Lichen^[(((Base == "Red" && Rufous == "Low") || (Base == "Cream" && Rufous == "High")) && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (Europe)]
      desc = Flavoplaca calcitrapa. Yellow lichen found in Europe.
    Lichen^[(((Base == "Red" && Rufous == "Low") || (Base == "Cream" && Rufous == "High")) && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || MidAm || SouthAm || Europe || British || NorthAf || SouthAf || WestAs || EastAs || SEastAs || Australia)]
      desc = Flavoplaca citrina (mealy firedot lichen). Yellow lichen growing on rock. Said to be cosmopolitan.
    Lichen^[(((Base == "Red" && Rufous == "Low") || (Base == "Cream" && Rufous == "High")) && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (Europe)]
      desc = Flavoplaca flavocitrina. Yellow lichen found in Europe.
    Lichen^[(((Base == "Red" && Rufous == "Low") || (Base == "Cream" && Rufous == "High")) && White != "HighWhite" && Albino == "Normal") && (Europe || NorthAf)]
      desc = Flavoplaca limonia. Mostly pale yellow lichen growing on rock. Initially thought to be a southern European species, it has since been shown to have a broader distribution, having been reported from Morocco, Denmark, and Sweden.
    Lichen^[(((Base == "Red" && Rufous == "Low") || (Base == "Cream" && Rufous == "High") || Base == "Green") && White == "NoWhite" && Albino == "Normal") && (Europe || British || Islands)]
      desc = Flavoplaca maritima. Yellow-green lichen growing on rocks. It occurs in the western British Isles, Western Europe, Mediterranean France, and the Channel Islands.
    Lichen^[(((Base == "Red" && Rufous == "Low") || (Base == "Cream" && Rufous == "High")) && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (Europe || WestAs || NorthAf)]
      desc = Flavoplaca oasis. Yellow lichen growing on rocks. Widespread across Europe, and has been reported in Western Asia (Syria) and North Africa.
    Lichen^[(((Base == "Red" && Rufous == "Low") || (Base == "Cream" && Rufous == "High")) && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (Europe || British)]
      desc = Flavoplaca ruderum. Yellow lichen growing on rocks or manmade structures.  It was long known from Spain in the south-west and northwards through France and Great Britain to Denmark; recent discoveries at three sites in Skåne, southern Sweden.
    //Flavopunctelia
    {Lichen^0.5|Greenshield}^[((Base == "Green") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || SouthAm || Europe || NorthAf || SouthAf || WestAs)]
      desc = Flavopunctelia flaventior (speckled greenshield). Pale green leafy lichen. Occurs in Asia, Europe, East Africa, North America, and South America.
    {Lichen^0.5|Greenshield}^[((Base == "Green" || (Base == "BlackTort" && Agouti == "Tabby" && !Silver)) && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || SouthAm)]
      desc = Flavopunctelia praesignis (fruiting speckled greenshield). Pale green leafy lichen with orange-brown fruiting structures. It is found in the southern United States, in various states of Mexico, and in South America. It has also been reported from Kenya, but that may be due to misidentification.
    {Lichen^0.5|Greenshield}^[((Base == "Green") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || SouthAm || Europe || SouthAf || WestAs || EastAs || Japan)]
      desc = Flavopunctelia soredica (powder-edged speckled greenshield). Pale green leafy lichen. It is widely distributed, having been recorded from North America, South America, South Africa, India, Russia, China and Japan.
    //Fulvophyton
    Lichen^[(((Base == "Cream") && (White == "HighWhite" || Albino == "Normal")) || Base == "White") && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Fulvophyton serusiauxii. Off-white lichen. Only known from its type locality in Mexico where it grows on granite boulders near the Pacific Ocean shore.
    //Fuscidea
    Lichen^[((Base == "Green") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Fuscidea appalachensis. Pale green lichen found on rock. Found in North America, the Appalachian Mountains in eastern North America, ranging from New Brunswick to Tennessee at the southern end.
    //Fuscopannaria
    Lichen^[((Base == "Black" || Base == "BlackTort") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || MidAm || SouthAm || Europe || NorthAf || SouthAf)]
      desc = Fuscopannaria leucosticta (rimmed shingle lichen). Dark grey lichen with small orange-brown spots. It is typically found growing on bark, although it has been occasionally recorded growing on rock, usually with mosses. Widely distributed in temperate eastern North America. Its distribution includes Central America and the Caribbean, extending as far south as Cuba. In Mexico, it is found in Chiapas. Reported from Ecuador, Tanzania, and Egypt into East Africa. Although very rare in Europe, was rediscovered there in Greece.

    //Gabura
    Lichen^[((Base == "Black" && Agouti != "Tabby") && (White == "LowWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (Islands)]
      desc = Gabura borbonica. Crumpled leafy lichen, black with white rims. Found on Réunion island. 
    Lichen^[((Base == "Green") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (Europe || British || NorthAf || WestAs || Australia || NewZeal)]
      desc = Gabura fascicularis. Dark green jelly lichen growing on trees. It occurs in oceanic and sub-oceanic regions of Europe and has been recorded in adjacent parts of North Africa and Asia. The species is also present in the Southern Hemisphere, having been documented in Australasia (including Australia and New Zealand).
    //Gallowayella
    Lichen^[(((Base == "Red" && Rufous == "Low") || (Base == "Cream" && Rufous == "High")) && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || Europe || British || WestAs || EastAs)]
      desc = Gallowayella fulva. Bright yellow lichen growing on bark. Widely distributed, occurring in Asia, Europe, and North America.
    Lichen^[(((Base == "Red" && Rufous == "Low") || (Base == "Cream" && Rufous == "High")) && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Gallowayella hasseana (poplar sunburst lichen). Golden lichen growing on bark. It occurs in North America. 
    Lichen^[(((Base == "Red") || (Base == "Cream" && Rufous == "High")) && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Gallowayella montana. Golden lichen growing on bark. Widely distributed in temperate regions of the western United States and Canada.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Green") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Gallowayella montana. Yellow-green lichen growing on bark and rock. It is native to North America, predominantly in the eastern regions, with its most significant population density in the Southeast.
    //Glaucomaria
    Lichen^[(Base == "White" || Base == "Cream" || Base == "Fawn" || Base == "FawnTort") && (NorthAm || Europe || British || NorthAf || SouthAf || WestAs || EastAs || NewZeal || Islands)]
      desc = Glaucomaria carpinea. Pale off-white lichen growing on bark. Recorded from Africa, Asia, Europe, Macaronesia, New Zealand, and North America.
    //Golubkovia
    Lichen^[((Base == "Red") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || WestAs)]
      desc = Golubkovia trachyphylla. Bright orange lichen growing on rock. Widely distributed lichen found in Asia and North America.
    {Lichen|{Witch's-hair|Witchhair}}^[((Base == "Blue" || (Base == "Black" && Agouti != "Solid")) && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || NewZeal || Antarctica)]
      desc = Gowardia nigricans (gray hair lichen or gray witch's hair). Greenish grey shrub-like lichen. In Antarctica, it is found in the South Orkney Islands. It has also been recorded from Greenland and New Zealand.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Red" || (Base == "Cream" && Rufous == "High") || Base == "Chocolate" || Base == "ChocolateTort" || Base == "Black" || Base == "BlackTort") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Gowardia zebrina. Golden to brown to black lichen. Only known to occur in coastal northwest North America, extending from the Insular Mountains of southern Vancouver Island north to Hazelton.
    //Graphis
    Lichen^[((Base == "Black" && (Agouti == "Tabby" && Silver)) && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || MidAm || Europe || Islands)]
      desc = Graphis crebra. White lichen with tiny black streaks and spots. In addition to the type locality in Guadeloupe, also known from St. Helena and the Galapagos. In 2011, it was reported from Florida in North America. In 2016, was reported from Portugal and in 2017 from the Seychelles.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Black" && (Agouti == "Tabby" && Silver)) && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || MidAm || SouthAm || SEastAs || Japan || Australia)]
      desc = Graphis desquamescens. White lichen with tiny black streaks and spots. Can be found in various countries including Brazil, Dominica, the United States, Mexico, and Japan. It also occurs in different parts of Australia such as Queensland, New South Wales, Victoria, and Tasmania. It was reported as new to Myanmar in 2020.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Black" && (Agouti == "Tabby" && Silver)) && Albino == "Normal") && (MidAm || SouthAm || Europe)]
      desc = Graphis plumierae. White lichen with tiny black streaks and spots. The type was collected in Gourbeyre, Guadeloupe. In 2016, reported from the Sintra Mountains, Portugal. It has also been documented from the Miranda region of Pantanal, Brazil.
    //Gyalolechia
    Lichen^[(((Base == "Red" && Rufous == "Low") || (Base == "Cream" && Rufous == "High")) && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || Europe)]
      desc = Gyalolechia bracteata (sulfur lichen). Golden fungus growing on ground. Found in some parts of Europe (Poland, Sweden), as well as across the United States.
    Lichen^[((Base == "CinnamonTort" || (Base == "Cinnamon" && Gold && Agouti == "Tabby" && !Silver)) && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || Europe || British || WestAs || Australia || NewZeal)]
      desc = Gyalolechia fulgens (scrambled egg lichen, yellow ground lichen). Pale yellow lichen with orange-brown spots. Grows on ground and moss. It is found across Europe and is widespread in the warmer regions of the Northern Hemisphere. The lichen is also present in Australia and New Zealand. In Wales, it seems to be restricted to coastal areas. Prominent component of the Negev desert. In North America, it is found in the interior of the continent with a range extending north to the Arctic.

    //Haematomma
    {Lichen|Bloodspot}^[((Base == "Red" || Base == "Cinnamon" || Base == "CinnamonTort") && (White == "HighWhite" || (Silver && Agouti == "Tabby"))) && (NorthAm || MidAm || SouthAm || NorthAf || SouthAf || EastAs || Australia || Islands)]
      desc = Haematomma accolens (tree bloodspot). Off white lichen with many small red spots. Occurs mainly in the southeastern United States. It has been recorded from North Carolina to northern Florida, with scattered occurrences extending westward to eastern Texas. Beyond North America, the species is also known from the West Indies, Costa Rica, Guatemala, Brazil, parts of Africa, and northeastern Australia. In Asia, it is known from Sri Lanka, China, and India.
    Lichen^[(((Base == "Red" || Base == "Cinnamon" || Base == "CinnamonTort") && (White == "HighWhite" || (Silver && Agouti == "Tabby"))) || Base == "White") && (NorthAm || Europe || British)]
      desc = Haematomma ochroleucum (yellow bloodstain lichen). White lichen, with tiny red specks. In Europe, reported as widespread. In parts of Ireland and Wales, it is rare but locally abundant on shaded rocky outcrops, particularly those that are north-facing. In Wales, it is more common inland than at the coast. In Belgium and Luxembourg, it is found primarily on protected, vertical surfaces on siliceous or sandstone rocks, or on the bark of older beech or oak trees in well-preserved forests. In North America, it is rare, and limited primarily to the Pacific Northwest and southern Rocky Mountains. There, it is found primarily in waterfall spray zones, with fewer colonies on drier vertical rock faces, rocky overhangs, and the trunks of large black cottonwood trees. It has also been found in Maine.
    //Hondaria
    Lichen^[((Base == "Black" && Agouti != "Tabby" && (!Silver || Agouti == "Solid")) && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (SouthAm)]
      desc = Hondaria leptospora. Black lichen growing on bark. Found predominantly in the west-central region of Brazil, particularly near the borders with Bolivia and Paraguay.
    //Hydropunctaria
    Lichen^[((Base == "Black" && Agouti != "Tabby" && (!Silver || Agouti == "Solid")) && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || Europe || British)]
      desc = Hydropunctaria amphibia. Black lichen growing on rock. Widely distributed in Europe, from Norway south to the Mediterranean and also on the Iberian coasts. In North America, documented from the Atlantic Coast, including the Nova Scotia's Bay of Fundy coast, the coast of Newfoundland and Labrador, and the Boston Harbor Islands National Recreation Area. On the west coast, it is known to occur in British Columbia.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Black" && Agouti != "Tabby" && (!Silver || Agouti == "Solid")) && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || Europe || British || Australia || NewZeal || Antarctica)]
      desc = Hydropunctaria maura (tar lichen). Black lichen growing on rock. It has a cosmopolitan distribution, and is found on both the East and West coasts of North America, and in the Southern Hemisphere in Tasmania and New Zealand.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Green") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (Europe || British)]
      desc = Hydropunctaria orae. Pale greenish lichen growing on rock. Documented from Wales, Ireland, and Norway.
    //Hypogymnia
    Lichen^[(Base == "White") && (EastAs || Islands)]
      desc = Hypogymnia flavida. Off-white branching lichen growing on wood and bark. In China, it has been recorded from Sichuan, Tibet, and Yunnan. It also occurs in Nepal and Taiwan.
    Lichen^[(Base == "White") && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Hypogymnia krogiae (freckled tube lichen). Off-white pale green branching lichen growing on wood and bark. Occurs in eastern North America from Tennessee and North Carolina, north to Quebec in Canada.
    Lichen^[(Base == "White") && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Hypogymnia occidentalis (lattice tube lichen). Off-white pale green branching lichen growing on wood and bark. Common in the Cascade Mountains and the northern Rocky Mountain area of the United States and Canada; its northern range extend to Alaska.
    Lichen^[(Base == "White") && (NorthAm || Europe || British || WestAs || EastAs)]
      desc = Hypogymnia physodes (monk's-hood lichen). Off-white pale green branching lichen growing on wood and bark. Common and widespread in the northern hemisphere.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Green") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (Europe || British)]
      desc = Hypogymnia tubulosa. Green branching lichen. Recorded in Scotland and Spain.
    //Hypotrachyna
    Lichen^[(Base == "White") && (NorthAm || MidAm || SouthAm || SouthAf || EastAs || SEastAs)]
      desc = Hypotrachyna catawbiensis (powder-tipped antler lichen). White branching lichen growing on rocks or bark. In North America, it grows in the mountains of western North Carolina and Virginia and eastern Tennessee, United States, extending north to Fundy National Park in New Brunswick, Canada. Found in east-central Mexico, and in Costa Rica, Venezuela and Ecuador. In Asia, it occurs in the Hengduan Mountains of China, and in the Baliem Valley of Papua New Guinea. It has also been recorded in Uganda.
    Lichen^[(Base == "White") && (NorthAm || MidAm || SouthAm || NorthAf || SouthAf || EastAs || Japan || SEastAs || Australia || Islands)]
      desc = Hypotrachyna osseoalba (grainy loop lichen). White leafy lichen. Found in subtropical and temperate areas of Asia (South Korea, Japan, Taiwan, and Thailand), Australia, Africa, Central America, South America, and the eastern United States.
    Lichen^[(Base == "White") && (NorthAm || British)]
      desc = Hypotrachyna taylorensis. White leafy lichen. Found in the Appalachians region of North America. It is also found in Britain and Ireland.
    
    //Igneoplaca
    Lichen^[((Base == "Red" || Base == "Cinnamon" || Base == "CinnamonTort") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Igneoplaca ignea. Red-orange lichen growing on rock. Found in Baja Mexico and in southern California.
    //Imshaugia
    Lichen^[((Base == "Lilac") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || Europe || EastAs)]
      desc = Imshaugia aleurites (salted starburst lichen). Pale grey-green leafy lichen growing on bark and wood of conifers. Widely distributed in Canada, the United States, and Europe. Also known from mainland China.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Green") && (White == "HighWhite")) && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Imshaugia placorodia (American starburst lichen). Silver grey leafy lichen with green-topped fruiting bodies. The North American distributionincludes eastern Canada and the northeastern United States, and areas of the central United States. In Mexico, it is found in the Northwest part of the country to its Central Volcanic Belt.

    //Kaernefeltia
    Lichen^[((Base == "Black" && Agouti != "Tabby" && (!Silver || Agouti == "Solid")) && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || Europe)]
      desc = Kaernefeltia merrillii (flattened thornbrush lichen). Black lichen growing on bark. Spans western North America, from southeastern Alaska and the Yukon southward through British Columbia to California, and reaches inland as far as western Montana. Most abundant in the region between the Cascade Range crest and the Continental Divide, particularly in the Siskiyou Mountains of southern Oregon and northern California. It does not occur along the immediate Pacific coastline. It has also been reported from northern Mexico and, disjunctly, from the central highlands of Spain.
    //Kalbionora
    Lichen^[((Base == "Blue") && (White == "HighWhite" || (Silver && Agouti != "Solid" && Tabby == "Spotted"))) && (SEastAs || Australia)]
      desc = Kalbionora palaeotropica. White lichen with green-grey spots growing on bark. Found in coastal forests in Thailand, Vietnam, and northeastern Australia.
    //Krogia
    Lichen^[((Base == "Green") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (Islands)]
      desc = Krogia macrophylla. Leafy green lichen. Found in New Caledonia.
    //Kuettlingeria
    Lichen^[(Base == "White") && (NorthAm || WestAs)]
      desc = Kuettlingeria albolutescens. White lichen growing on rock, including cement and bricks. It occurs in Europe and Western Asia.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Red") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || Europe || British)]
      desc = Kuettlingeria atroflava. Orange lichen growing as spots on rock. In North America, it has been recorded from California and Colorado in the United States, and British Columbia in Canada. Also found in Europe.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Cinnamon" || Base == "Chocolate") && (White == "HighWhite" || (Silver && Agouti != "Solid" && Tabby == "Spotted"))) && (Europe || NorthAf || WestAs)]
      desc = Kuettlingeria erythrocarpa. White lichen with red-brown spots. Found in the Mediterranian region, and Armenia, Iraq, and Israel.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Cinnamon" || Base == "Red") && (White == "HighWhite" || (Silver && Agouti != "Solid" && Tabby == "Spotted"))) && (Europe || British || WestAs || Islands)]
      desc = Kuettlingeria neotaurica. White lichen with small red freckles growing on rock. Grows near sea coasts throughout the Mediterranean and Black Sea regions, extending along Europe's Atlantic coast to Great Britain. 
    Lichen^[(Base == "White") && (Europe || British || NorthAf || SouthAf || WestAs || EastAs)]
      desc = Kuettlingeria teicholyta. White lichen growing on rock. Recorded from Africa, Asia, and Europe. 
    //Kurokawia
    Lichen^[((Base == "Green" || (Base == "Black" && Agouti == "Tabby" && Tabby == "Spotted" && !Silver)) && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || EastAs)]
      desc = Kurokawia palmulata (shaggy fringe lichen). Leafy green lichen with black spots growing on bark. Endemic to eastern North America and eastern Asia.

    //Lecanographa
    Lichen^[(Base == "Blue" && White != "NoWhite") && (Islands)]
      desc = Lecanographa dialeuca. Mottled grey & white lichen growing on rock. It is found in Cape Verde and Sálvora Island.
    //Lecanora
    Lichen^[(((Base == "BlackTort" && Agouti == "Tabby" && !Silver)) && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || Europe || British || WestAs || Islands)]
      desc = Lecanora albellula. Green lichen with orange freckles. Widely distributed across Asia, Europe, and North America.
    Lichen^[(Base == "Blue" && White == "LowWhite" && Albino == "Normal") && (British || Islands)]
      desc = Lecanora cenisia. White-edged grey lichen growing on rock. It is recorded from the Channel and Scilly Islands and appears in scattered populations throughout Britain's upland areas.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Black" || Base == "BlackTort") && Agouti == "Tabby" && Tabby == "Ticked" && Silver) && (British || Europe)]
      desc = Lecanora cinereofusca. White to greenish lichen with dense brown speckling. Grows in the United Kingdom and the Alps.
    Lichen^[(Base == "Green" && White != "NoWhite") && (NorthAm || Europe || British || Islands)]
      desc = Lecanora confusa. Pale green & white lichen growing on bark. Widespread in Northern and Western Europe, with a range extending to southern Scandinavia. It also occurs in North America (including Alaska), in Macaronesia, and in Paramushir in the Russian Far East.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Black") && (White == "HighWhite")) && (NewZeal || Antarctica)]
      desc = Lecanora epibryon. Black-tipped white lichen growing in tube shapes on soil and grass. Found in New Zealand and Antarctica (and possibly worldwide?).
    Lichen^[((Base == "Red") && Agouti == "Tabby" && Tabby == "Ticked" && Silver) && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Lecanora louisianae. White lichen with dense yellow speckling. It is common and widespread in the Coastal Plain region of southeastern North America.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Chocolate" || Base == "ChocolateTort" || Base == "Cinnamon" || Base == "CinnamonTort") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Lecanora mellea. Orange-brown lichen growing on rock. Found in North America.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Cream") && (White == "NoWhite")) && (NorthAm || SouthAm || Europe || British || NorthAf || SouthAf || WestAs || EastAs || SEastAs || Australia || NewZeal || Islands)]
      desc = Lecanora muralis. Pale yellow-green lichen growing on rock. It grows all over the world including in Europe, Asia, North America, South America, Africa, Macaronesia, Oceania, and Australasia.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Green") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || MidAm || SouthAm || Europe || British || NorthAf || SouthAf || WestAs || EastAs || SEastAs || Japan || Australia || NewZeal || Hawaii || Islands || Antarctica)]
      desc = Lecanora polytropa (granite-speck rim lichen). Pale green lichen growing on rock. Cosmopolitan distribution, and is known from all continents. It is found in the maritime and continental Antarctic, including the Antarctic Peninsula, Queen Mary Land, and Victoria Land.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Cream" || Base == "Red") && (White == "NoWhite")) && (NorthAm || SouthAm || Europe || British || NewZeal || Antarctica)]
      desc = Lecanora stenotropa. Pale yellow-green lichen growing on rock. It is widespread in the United Kingdom, Germany, Poland, Spain, and Italy. It was recorded from Antarctica. Also occurs in North America (Canada), South America (Bolivia), and New Zealand.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Green") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || SouthAm || Europe || NorthAf || WestAs || Islands)]
      desc = Lecanora strobilina (mealy rim lichen). Pale green lichen growing on bark. It is distributed across North America and the Mediterranean but has become established in South America and the Galapagos.
    Lichen^[(Base == "Lilac" && White == "LowWhite" && Albino == "Normal") && (British || Islands)]
      desc = Lecanora subcarnea. White-edged pale grey lichen growing on rock. It has been reliably reported from Westmorland in England, northern Wales, central and eastern Scotland, and the Channel Islands
    Lichen^[(Base == "Lilac" && White == "LowWhite" && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || MidAm || SouthAm || WestAs || EastAs || Japan || SEastAs || Australia || NewZeal)]
      desc = Lecanora subimmergens. White-edged pale grey lichen growing on rock. It occurs in Asia, America, and Australasia.
    //Lecidea
    Lichen^[((Base == "BlackTort" || (Base == "Black" && Agouti == "Tabby" && Tabby == "Spotted" && !Silver && Gold == "None")) && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Lecidea atrobrunnea. Orange-brown lichen with black spots. Most abundant in mountains of the continental western United States and Alaska.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Blue" || Base == "BlueTort" || Base == "Lilac" || Base == "LilacTort") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || Europe || NorthAf || WestAs || EastAs)]
      desc = Lecidea fuscoatra. Grey lichen growing on rock. Reported from Europe, North Africa, North America, and Asia.
    Lichen^[((Base == "BlackTort" || (Base == "Black" && Agouti == "Tabby" && Tabby == "Spotted" && !Silver && Gold == "None")) && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Lecidea perlatolica. Orange-brown lichen with black spots. It has been recorded from the western United States: California (Butte, El Dorado, Inyo, Los Angeles, Mono, San Bernardino, Tulare, and Tuolumne counties), Utah, and Nevada.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Black" && Agouti == "Tabby" && Tabby == "Spotted" && Silver)) && (NorthAm || Europe || WestAs || EastAs || Antarctica)]
      desc = Lecidea tessellata. White lichen with black spots growing on rock. In northern North America, it is common and widely distributed. It also occurs in Afghanistan, China, Nepal, Europe, and Russian Asia. In India, it has been recorded only from the alpine Western Himalayas. Its southern distribution extends to James Ross Island, where it is locally common.
    //Leifidium
    Lichen^[(Base == "White") && (SouthAm || Australia || NewZeal || Islands)]
      desc = Leifidium tenerum. Leafy white lichen. Spans from Cape Horn north to Temuco in Chile, through New Zealand, from Tasmania to central New South Wales in Australia, and across several subantarctic islands.
    //Lepidocollema
    Lichen^[(Base == "Blue" || Base == "Lilac" || (Agouti != "Tabby" && Base == "Black")) && (SEastAs || Islands)]
      desc = Lepidocollema marianum. Grey lichen. Occurs in Asia (including Thailand, Sri Lanka, and Taiwan) and Mauritius.
    //Lepraria
    Lichen^[((Base == "Blue" || Base == "Lilac") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Lepraria caesiella. Pale blue-green lichen growing on bark. Found in northeastern North America, extending southward in the Appalachian Mountains.
    Lichen^[(Base == "White") && (NorthAm || Europe || Islands)]
      desc = Lepraria elobata. Off-white lichen growing on rock. It occurs in Europe, North America, and Greenland.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Blue" || Base == "Green") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Lepraria harrisiana. Blue-green lichen growing on bark. Found in North America, from Massachusetts to Georgia, westward to at least Alabama, and the in disjunct populations in the southern Appalachian Mountains, long the edges of the Ozarks and the Ouachita Mountains, the Canadian Maritimes, and the Great Lakes Region.
    Lichen^[(Base == "White") && (Europe || Islands)]
      desc = Lepraria isidiata. White lichen growing on rock. Recorded in Mediterranian Europe.
    Lichen^[(Base == "White" || Base == "Green") && (NorthAm || Europe || WestAs || EastAs || SEastAs || Australia)]
      desc = Lepraria jackii. Pale green to white lichen growing on bark. Recorded across Europe, North America, Asia, and Australia.
    Lichen^[(Base == "White") && (SouthAm)]
      desc = Lepraria nothofagi. White lichen growing on bark. Known only in the Andean–Patagonian forests of Neuquén Province, Argentina.
    Lichen^[(Base == "White") && (NorthAm || Europe)]
      desc = Lepraria xerophila. White lichen typically growing on soil. Found in Europe and northwestern North America.
    //Leprocaulon
    Lichen^[(Base == "White") && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Leprocaulon adhaerens. White lichen typically growing on rocks. Known from coastal southern California, Pennsylvania, and Missouri.
    //Leproplaca
    Lichen^[(((Base == "Red" && Rufous == "Low") || (Base == "Cream" && Rufous == "High")) && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (Europe || British || WestAs || NewZeal)]
      desc = Leproplaca chrysodeta. Bright yellow powdery lichen growing on rock. Found across the British Isles, throughout many regions in Europe, as well as in the Middle East and New Zealand.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Red") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || SouthAm || Europe || British || NorthAf || SouthAf || WestAs || EastAs  || Australia)]
      desc = Leproplaca cirrochroa. Orange lichen growing in a ring formation on rock. Recorded from Africa, Asia, Australia, Europe, and North and South America.
    //Leptogium
    {Lichen^0.5|Jellyskin}^[((Base == "Green" || ((Base == "BlackTort" || Base == "Chocolate") && Agouti == "Tabby")) && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || MidAm || SouthAm)]
      desc = Leptogium chloromelum (ruffled jellyskin). Green lichen with brown spots. Found across the American tropics, from as far north as New England, and down to South America (Brazil, Peru).
    {Lichen^0.5|Jellyskin}^[((Base == "Blue") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || SouthAm || Europe || British || SEastAs || Islands)]
      desc = Leptogium cyanescens (blue jellyskin). Blue-grey leafy lichen. In North America it is frequent in southern Canada through the eastern United States, extending westward into British Columbia. European records span from the British Isles and Fennoscandia to the Mediterranean; also documented in Chile, the Galápagos, Madeira and South-East Asia.
    {Lichen^0.5|Jellyskin}^[((Base == "Black" || Base == "BlackTort") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || WestAs)]
      desc = Leptogium rivulare (flooded jellyskin lichen). Rare black lichen with light brown spots found only in Republics of Marii El and Komi, Russia, and in Ontario, Canada.
    //Letharia
    Lichen^[((Base == "Green") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Letharia columbiana (brown-eye wolf lichen). Shrub-like green lichen growing on bark. Found in the Pacific Northwest of the United States, and parts of Canada.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Green") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || Europe)]
      desc = Letharia vulpina (wolf lichen). Shrub-like green lichen growing on bark. Grows in parts of western and continental Europe and the Pacific Northwest and northern Rocky Mountains of North America.
    //Lethariella
    Lichen^[(((Base == "Red" && Rufous == "Low") || (Base == "Cream" && Rufous == "High")) && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (Islands)]
      desc = Lethariella canariensis. Golden yellow lichen growing in long strands. Found in the Canary Islands.
    //Leucodermia
    Lichen^[((Base == "Green") && (White == "NoWhite" || White == "LowWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || MidAm || SouthAf || Islands)]
      desc = Leucodermia leucomelos. Pale yellowish-green branching lichen. In the Americas extends from Belleville, Ontario in the north, south to Mexico and Central America. Found across eastern Africa, and in South Africa. Found in the Canary Islands and the Azores.
    //Lichenomphalia
    {Lichen|Mushroom}^[(((Base == "Red" && Rufous == "Low") || (Base == "Cream" && Rufous == "High")) && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (Austrlia)]
      desc = Lichenomphalia chromacea. Bright yellow lichen resembling a mushroom. Found in South Australia, New South Wales, and Tasmania.
    {Lichen|Mushroom}^[((Base == "Green" || (Base == "BlackTort" && Agouti == "Tabby" && !Silver && Gold == "None")) && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || Europe || British || WestAs || EastAs)]
      desc = Lichenomphalia hudsoniana. Green leafy lichen, with yellow mushroom-like fruiting bodies. It occurs in Asia, Europe, and North America, largely in alpine and arctic regions, but is also known from areas near the ocean in Norway and Great Britain.
    {Lichen|Mushroom|Agaric}^[((Base == "Cream") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || Europe || WestAs || EastAs)]
      desc = Lichenomphalia umbellifera (lichen agaric, green-pea mushroom lichen). Has cream mushroom-type fruiting bodies. Found across the Northern Hemisphere, especially the Arctic.
    {Lichen|Mushroom}^[((Base == "Lilac" || Base == "LilacTort") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || Europe || EastAs || Islands)]
      desc = Lichenomphalia velutina. Has grey-brown mushroom-type fruiting bodies. Found in North America, Europe, China, and Greenland.
    //Lichinella
    Lichen^[((Base == "Black" && Agouti != "Tabby") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || SouthAm || Europe || NorthAf || WestAs || Islands)]
      desc = Lichinella iodopulchra. Dark grey lichen growing on rock. In North America it is recorded from the south-western United States and north-western Mexico (with specific Sonoran occurrences in Arizona and Baja California Sur); in Macaronesia it is recorded from the Canary Islands; in the Mediterranean basin it occurs in south-eastern Spain and in North Africa (including Algeria); it extends through the Middle East (e.g., Iran) and into the Caucasus (Georgia); and has been verified from north-eastern Brazil.
    //Lithothelium
    Lichen^[(Base == "White") && (NewZeal)]
      desc = Lithothelium kiritea. White lichen growing on bark. Found in New Zealand.
    //Lobaria
    {Lichen|Specklebelly}^[((Base == "Black" || Base == "Chocolate" || Base == "Cinnamon" || Base == "Blue" || Base == "Ginger") && (White == "LowWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Lobaria anomala (netted specklebelly). Light brown to black, with white patterns, leafy lichen growing on bark. Found along the Pacific coast of the United States and Canada. Its range extends north from Alaska, through British Columbia, south to California.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Green") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (Islands)]
      desc = Lobaria macaronesica. Green leafy lichen growing on bark. Found in Macaronesia.
    {Lichen|Lungwort}^[((Base == "Green") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Lobaria oregana (lettuce lichen, Oregon lungwort). Light green leafy lichen growing on trees. Spans from Southern Oregon and northern California up into Alaska, around and into the Kenai Peninsula.
    {Lichen|Lungwort|Moss|Lungs}^[((Base == "Green") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || Europe || British || SouthAf || WestAs || EastAs)]
      desc = Lobaria pulmonaria (tree lungwort, lung lichen, lung moss, lungwort lichen, oak lungs, oak lungwort). Green leafy lichen growing on trees. It has a wide distribution in Europe, Asia, North America and Africa.
    {Lichen|Lungwort}^[((Base == "Green" || (Base == "BlackTort" && Agouti == "Tabby")) && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || SouthAm || EastAs)]
      desc = Lobaria quercizans (smooth lungwort). Green leafy lichen with red-brown fruiting bodies growing on trees. Found in eastern North America, South America (Bolivia), eastern Asia (China, Korea, Outer Manchuria). In eastern North America, it is found from Newfoundland to northern Georgia and west to eastern Minnesota. An outlying population is found in the Ouachita Mountains. 
    {Lichen|Lungwort}^[((Base == "Blue" || Base == "Lilac" || Base == "Cream") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || Europe || British || SouthAf || Islands)]
      desc = Lobaria scrobiculata (textured lungwort). Grey or pale yellow leafy lichen growing on bark. Found in temperate climates, especially coastal districts of north west Europe, north eastern North America and north western North America, but there are also a few known occurrences in warmer countries such as Kenya. The distribution records are possibly very incomplete and biased towards Europe and North America.
    //Lobariella
    Lichen^[((Base == "Green" || (Base == "BlackTort" && Agouti == "Tabby")) && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (MidAm || SouthAm)]
      desc = Lobariella pallida. Green leafy lichen with orange-brown spots. Occurs in páramo regions of Central and South America.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Green") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (SouthAm)]
      desc = Lobariella reticulata. Green leafy lichen. Found in Colombia.
    //Lobothallia
    Lichen^[(Base == "White" || Base == "Cream") && (NorthAm || Europe || WestAs)]
      desc = Lobothallia alphoplaca (variable sunken disk lichen). Pale creamy lichen growing on rock. It is found in Europe, central Asia, and North America, where it grows in the southwestern deserts to central California.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Chocolate" || Base == "Black" || Base == "Blue") && (Albino != "Normal" || White == "MidWhite" || White == "HighWhite")) && (NorthAm || Europe || WestAs || EastAs)]
      desc = Lobothallia praeradiosa. White or pale creamy lichen with brown patches, grows on rock. Found broadly across Eurasia, and in North America.
    //Loxospora
    Lichen^[((Base == "Green" || (Base == "BlackTort" && Agouti == "Tabby")) && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Loxospora ochrophaea. Green lichen with orange-brown spots growing on bark. Found in North America.

    //Malmidea
    Lichen^[((Base == "Green") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (MidAm)]
      desc = Malmidea furfurosa. Dark green lichen growing on bark. Found in Cuba.
    //Megalaria
    Lichen^[((Base == "Green" || (Base == "Black" && Agouti == "Tabby" && (Tabby == "Spotted" || Tabby == "Ticked") && !Silver && Gold == "None")) && (White == "NoWhite" || White == "LowWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NewZeal)]
      desc = Megalaria crispisulcans. Pale green lichen with a white rim and black speckling. Grows on bark. Endemic to New Zealand.
    //Melanelia
    {Lichen|{Brown-s|S}hield}^[((Base == "Chocolate" || (Base == "Black" && Agouti == "Tabby")) && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || Europe || WestAs || EastAs || Islands)]
      desc = Melanelia hepatizon (rimmed camouflage lichen, rimmed brown-shield). Dark brown lichen growing on rocks. Found in Europe, the Russian Arctic. In North America found in the Pacific Northwest and the Rocky Mountains extending north to Alaska and other arctic regions in the west, and the Appalachians and Great Lakes regions in the east. Range includes China, Iceland, and Greenland.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Chocolate" || (Base == "Black" && Agouti == "Tabby")) && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || Europe || British)]
      desc = Melanelia stygia (alpine camouflage lichen). Dark brown lichen growing on rocks. Found across North America and Europe, including the British Isles.
    //Melanelixia
    Lichen^[((Base == "Green") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || WestAs || EastAs)]
      desc = Melanelixia albertana (powder-rimmed camouflage lichen). Dark green lichen growing on bark. Found in North America, northern Mongolia, Transbaikal, Yakutia, the Caucasus, and parts of China.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Green") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Melanelixia californica (California camouflage lichen). Green lichen growing on bark. Found primarily in southern California, also reported in Oregon.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Chocolate" || Base == "Green" || (Base == "Black" && Agouti == "Tabby")) && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (Europe || British || EastAs || Japan || NorthAf)]
      desc = Melanelixia fuliginosa. Green or brown lichen growing on rock. Found across Europe, including the British Isles. In Asia, reported in temperate parts of Russia, East Asia, and Central Asia – for instance, in Siberia, Korea, and Japan. Some records also exist from North Africa (e.g. Atlas Mountains).
    //Melanohalea
    {Lichen|{Brown-s|S}hield}^[((Base == "Green") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || MidAm || Europe || British || Islands)]
      desc = Melanohalea exasperatula (lustrous camouflage lichen, lustrous brown-shield). Leafy green lichen growing on bark. Widely found in North America, Central America, Europe, Macaronesia.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Green") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || EastAs)]
      desc = Melanohalea halei. Dull green lichen growing on bark. Found primarily across North America, with records in China.
    {Lichen|Shield}^[((Base == "Chocolate" || Base == "Cinnamon" || (Base == "Black" && Agouti == "Tabby")) && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || Europe || British || WestAs || EastAs || islands)]
      desc = Melanohalea olivacea (spotted camouflage lichen, spotted brown shield). Brown lichen growing on bark. Found across the northern hemisphere.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Green" || (Base == "Black" && Agouti == "Tabby")) && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || EastAs)]
      desc = Melanohalea subelegantula. Brown-green lichen growing on bark. Known in North America and Tibet.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Green") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Melanohalea subolivacea (brown-eyed camouflage lichen). Dark green lichen growing on bark. Largely North American.
    //Menegazzia
    Lichen^[((Base == "Red") && (White != "HighWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (Australia || NewZeal)]
      desc = Menegazzia castanea. Golden lichen growing on rock. Found in Australia and New Zealand.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Green") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (Australia || NewZeal)]
      desc = Menegazzia eperforata. Leafy green lichen. Found in Australia and New Zealand.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Green") && (White != "HighWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (Australia || NewZeal)]
      desc = Menegazzia nothofagi. Pale green lichen. Found in Australia and New Zealand.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Green") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (SouthAm || Australia || NewZeal)]
      desc = Menegazzia pertransita. Pale green lichen. Found in Australia, New Zealand, and South America.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Green") && (White == "NoWhite" || White == "LowWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || MidAm || SouthAm || Europe || British || WestAs || EastAs || SEastAs || Japan || Hawaii || Islands)]
      desc = Menegazzia subsimilis. Bright green lichen.  Found scattered across the world, including Oceania (Hawaii, Solomon Islands), Asia (Japan, Papua New Guinea, Russia, Tibet, Malaysia and Indonesia), Europe (Austria, Germany, Portugal, the British Isles), South America (Ecuador, Peru), the Caribbean (Dominican Republic, Jamaica) and North America (Canada, USA).
    Lichen^[((Base == "Green") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || MidAm || Europe || British || WestAs || EastAs)]
      desc = Menegazzia terebrata. Pale green lichen. Found in North America, Central America (Costa Rica), the Carribean (Dominican Republic, Haiti), Europe (Austria, England, Ireland, Italy, Norway, Scotland, Sweden), Asia (China, Turkey).
    Lichen^[((Base == "Green" || (Base == "BlackTort" && Agouti == "Tabby")) && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (Australia || NewZeal)]
