    //Omphalora
    Lichen^[((Base == "BlackTort") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Omphalora arizonica. Orange and black lichen. Restricted to high-elevation areas in Arizona, Colorado, and New Mexico. Critically endangered.

    //Pannaria
    Lichen^[((Base == "Green") && (White == "LowWhite" || White == "MidWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NewZeal || Islands)]
      desc = Pannaria fulvescens. Dark green ruffled lichen with white trimmed edges. It occurs in French Polynesia and in New Zealand.
    //Pannoparmelia
    Lichen^[((Base == "Black") && (White == "HighWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (SouthAm || Australia || NewZeal)]
      desc = Pannoparmelia angustata. Greenish off-white leafy lichen with a black underside. Found in southeastern Australia (New South Wales, Australian Capital Territory, Victoria, and Tasmania) as well as New Zealand and southern South America (Argentina and Chile).
    //Parmelia
    Lichen^[((Base == "Green") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || Europe || NorthAf || WestAs)]
      desc = Parmelia barrenoae. Green leafy lichen. Occurring in Europe, western North America (California, Idaho, Oregon, and Washington), Africa, and Asia. 
    Lichen^[(((Base == "Black") && Agouti != "Tabby" && (!Silver || Agouti == "Solid")) && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (Europe || British || WestAs)]
      desc = Parmelia discordans. Black lichen growing on rock. Within Europe it has been reported from Belgium, Germany, Denmark, Spain, France, Finland, the United Kingdom, Ireland, Norway, the Netherlands, Poland, Russia, Sweden, and Turkey.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Lilac")) && (Europe || Islands)]
      desc = Parmelia ernstiae. Light greenish grey lichen. Found across Europe, and in Madeira.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Lilac")) && (NorthAm || SouthAm || Europe || NorthAf || SouthAf || WestAs || EastAs)]
      desc = Parmelia omphalodes. Light greenish grey lichen. Recorded in Asia, Africa, Europe, and North and South Americas.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Lilac")) && (NorthAm || SouthAm || Europe || NewZeal || Antarctica)]
      desc = Parmelia pinnatifida. Grey leafy lichen. Found across Europe, North America, and possibly South America, New Zealand, and Antarctica.
    {Lichen|Crottle}^[((Base == "Green" || Base == "BlackTort" && Agouti == "Tabby") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (Europe || British)]
      desc = Parmelia saxatilis (salted shield lichen, crottle). Pale grey-green leafy lichen. Found in Scotland.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Green") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || EastAs || Japan)]
      desc = Parmelia squarrosa (bottlebrush shield lichen). Leafy green lichen. Widely found in North America, primarily in the eastern region including the Great Lakes-Appalachian area, as well as in western North America. It is also widespread in eastern Asia, with reports of its occurrence in Japan, China, North Korea, South Korea, the Russian Far East, and Nepal.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Lilac" || Base == "White")) && (NorthAm || Europe || SouthAm || NorthAf)]
      desc = Parmelia sulcata (hammered shield lichen, cracked-shield lichen). Light greenish grey lichen. Very common across North America, found in Europe, Chile, Kenya, Ethiopia.
    Lichen^[(Base == "White") && (Europe || British)]
      desc = Parmelina pastillifera. Pale off-white grey leafy lichen. Found in Europe and Great Britain.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Chocolate" || Base == "Black" && Agouti == "Tabby") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (Europe)]
      desc = Parmelina quercina. Brown lichen growing in clusters of circular discs on bark. Found in continental Europe.
    //Parmotrema
    Lichen^[(Base == "White") && (NorthAm || SouthAm || Europe || NorthAf || SouthAf || Australia || NewZeal || Islands)]
      desc = Parmotrema arnoldii (powdered ruffle lichen). Off-white lichen. Recorded in Africa, Asia, Europe, Oceania, Macaronesia, and North and South America.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Green") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || SouthAm || SouthAf || SEastAs)]
      desc = Parmotrema gardneri. Pale green spiky lichen. In addition to South America, it is also found in Africa, Asia, and North America.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Green") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || MidAm || SouthAm || SouthAf || Japan || SEastAs || Australia || Islands)]
      desc = Parmotrema mellissii. Pale green lichen. It has been found in Saint Helena, the southern U.S.A., the Neotropics from Mexico to Colombia and Brazil, Africa (including the Canary Islands and Kenya), Asia (Japan, Laos, the Philippines), Australia and Oceania.
    Lichen^[(Base == "White") && (NorthAm || SouthAm || Europe || British || NorthAf || SouthAf || EastAs || Japan || Australia || Islands)]
      desc = Parmotrema perlatum (powdered ruffle lichen). White leafy lichen. It has been reported across numerous European countries including Austria, Belgium, the Czech Republic, France, Germany, Great Britain, Ireland, Italy, Luxembourg, the Netherlands, Portugal, Scandinavia, Slovakia, Spain, and Ukraine. Beyond Europe, it is also present in Macaronesia, Africa, Australia, North America, and South America. Its Asian distribution includes India, Japan, Taiwan, and South Korea.
    Lichen^[(Base == "White" || (Base == "Black" && (White == "HighWhite" || (Silver && Tabby == "Ticked" && Gold == "Wideband")))) && (NorthAm || MidAm || SouthAm || Europe || British || SouthAf || EastAs || Japan || SEastAs || Australia || NewZeal || Hawaii || Islands)]
      desc = Parmotrema reticulatum (Black sheet lichen). Off-white lichen with black underside. Found just about worldwide, outside of tropical rainforest and arid regions regions.
    Lichen^[(Base == "White") && (MidAm || SouthAm || Europe || EastAs || SEastAs || Australia || NewZeal || Islands)]
      desc = Parmotrema robustum. White leafy lichen. Reported from Europe, eastern Australia, New Zealand, India, Thailand, Papua New Guinea, Macaronesia, and the Neotropics, including Bolivia, Brazil, Colombia, Costa Rica, Ecuador, and Venezuela.
    Lichen^[(Base == "White") && (NorthAm || MidAm || Europe || SouthAf || EastAs)]
      desc = Parmotrema stuppuem (powder-edged ruffle lichen). Pale off-white green leafy lichen. Found across North America with a majority of samples being collected in and around the Great Lakes region of the United States. It also occurs in Europe, southern Africa, southern Asia, and Central America.
    Lichen^[(Base == "White") && (NorthAm || MidAm || SouthAm || SEastAs)]
      desc = Parmotrema submarginale. Off-white leafy lichen. It is found in Bolivia, Brazil, Costa Rica, Thailand, and the United States.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Green") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || Islands)]
      desc = Parmotrema xanthinum. Pale green leafy lichen. Found in regions of southeastern North America, including the Coastal plain, Piedmont, southern Appalachian Mountains, and Ozark Highlands. It is also known from various subtropical and tropical regions globally, including Madagascar.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Green") && (White == "HighWhite")) && (NorthAm || MidAm || SouthAm || SouthAf || SEastAs || Australia)]
      desc = Parmotrema zollingeri. White lichen with pale teal edges. Recorded in Australia, East Africa, North, Central, and South America, and Southeast Asia.
    //Parvoplaca
