      desc = Parvoplaca tiroliensis. Black lichen with orange spots. Recorded in Iraq, Greenland, Medny Island (Russian far east).
    //Peltigera
    {Lichen|Frecklepelt}^[((Base == "BlackTort" && Agouti == "Tabby" && Tabby == "Spotted" && !Silver)) && (NorthAm || Europe || WestAs || EastAs)]
      desc = Peltigera aphthosa ( green dog lichen, leafy lichen, felt lichen, common freckle pelt). Lichen with cup-shaped creamy fruiting bodies with green, black-spotted insides. Found throughout the Arctic, boreal, and temperate regions of the Northern Hemisphere.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Green") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || Europe)]
      desc = Peltigera britannica. Green leafy lichen. It is native to Europe and North America.
    Lichen^[((Base == "BlackTort" || (Base == "Black" && Agouti == "Tabby")) && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || Europe || WestAs || EastAs || Antarctica)]
      desc = Peltigera castanea (chestnut pelt lichen). Black-and-brown mushroom-like lichen. Known from northwestern North America; Russia and Estonia; Mount Xiaowutai, Hebei, China; James Ross Island in the Antarctic Peninsula.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Cinnamon" || Base == "Chocolate") && (White == "NoWhite" || White == "LowWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Peltigera cinnamomea (cinnamon-pelt lichen). Brown mushroom-like lichen. Found across western North America. 
    Lichen^[((Base == "LilacTort" || Base == "Lilac") && (White == "NoWhite" || White == "LowWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (SouthAm)]
      desc = Peltigera hydrophila. Warm grey lichen. Found across Chile, extending from Los Ríos Region and Los Lagos Region to the southernmost tip of Magallanes Region.
    {Lichen|Waterfan}^[(((Base == "Black") && Agouti != "Tabby" && (!Silver || Agouti == "Solid")) && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Peltigera hydrothyria (waterfan). Black lichen growing by water. Found across North America as different varieties in different regions.
    {Lichen|Frecklepelt}^[((Base == "Green") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || Europe || WestAs || EastAs || Islands)]
      desc = Peltigera leucophlebia (ruffled freckled pelt). Bright green leafy lichen. Found in North America, Asia, and Europe.
    {Lichen|Saddlepelt}^[((Base == "Blue" || (Base == "Black" && Agouti != "Solid" && Rufous == "Low")) && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || Europe || WestAs || EastAs)]
      desc = Peltigera neckeri (black saddle pelt). Grey lichen with black-tipped spikes. Found throughout North America, Europe, and Asia.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Blue") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || Europe || WestAs || EastAs)]
      desc = Peltigera praetextata (scaly dog pelt lichen). Grey lichen found on moss and bark. Native to North America, Europe, and Asia. 
    Lichen^[((Base == "Blue" || Base == "BlueTort") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || Europe || WestAs || EastAs)]
      desc = Peltigera retifoveata. Grey lichen with a cream underside found on the grown or with moss. Uncommon in Europe, having been recorded from only a few locations in Scandinavia. There are also records from the Russian Far East and Siberia. The lichen is more common in northern North America, with a range extending from subarctic regions (Alaska, Yukon, and the Northwest Territories, and including several western Canadian provinces: British Columbia, Alberta, and Manitoba. The southern extent of its North American range reaches Washington.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Green") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || Europe || WestAs || EastAs)]
      desc = Peltigera venosa (fan lichen). Leafy green lichen with brown-black fruiting bodies. Found in temperate and boreal regions of North America, Europe, and Asia.
    //Peltula
    {Lichen|Rock-olive}^[((Base == "Black" || Base == "Blue") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || MidAm || SouthAm || Europe || NorthAf || SouthAf || WestAs || EastAs || Australia)]
      desc = Peltula euploca (powdery rock-olive). Grey lichen growing on rock. With a cosmopolitan distribution, Peltula euploca is the most widespread species of Peltula: it has been recorded from all continents except Antarctica and is especially common in subtropical and tropical arid regions.
    //Pertusaria
    Lichen^[(Base == "White") && (NewZeal)]
      desc = Pertusaria allanii. White lichen growing on rock in New Zealand.
    //Pertusaria
    Lichen^[(Base == "White" || ((Base == "Red" && Rufous == "Low") || (Base == "Cream" && Rufous == "High"))) && (British || Europe)]
      desc = Pertusaria flavida. White to yellow lichen growing on bark. Widespread throughout southern and eastern Britain, parts of Wales, Scotland, and Ireland, as well as mountainous regions of Spain and Portugal.
    Lichen^[(Base == "White" || Base == "Green") && (Europe || WestAs || EastAs || SouthAf)]
      desc = Pertusaria pertusa. White to blueish green lichen growing on bark. Native to Eurasia and Southern Africa.
    Lichen^[(Base == "Cream" && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (Europe)]
      desc = Pertusaria rupicola. Pale yellow lichen growing on rock in Spain, France, and Bulgaria.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Green") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Pertusaria texana (Texas wart lichen). Pale green bumpy lichen growing on bark. It is found in Mexico and the southwestern United States.
    //Phaeophyscia
    Lichen^[((Base == "Green") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (Europe)]
      desc = Phaeophyscia endophoenicea. Green lichen growing on bark. Found across Europe.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Green") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Phaeophyscia leana (Lea's bog lichen). Green leafy lichen growing on bark. It is extant in six states, including Alabama, Illinois, Indiana, Kentucky, Ohio, and Tennessee, where it grows by the Ohio river.
    {Lichen|Shadow}^[((Base == "Black" && Agouti == "Tabby" && !Silver && Gold == "None") && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || Europe || NorthAf || SouthAf || WestAs || EastAs)]
      desc = Phaeophyscia sciastra (dark shadow lichen, five o'clock shadow). Green and black lichen growing on rock. Found in Africa, Asia, Europe, and North America. 
    //Phlyctis
    Lichen^[(Base == "White") && (NorthAm || Europe || NorthAf || SouthAf || WestAs || EastAs)]
      desc = Phlyctis argena. White lichen growing on bark. Widespread, including in Africa, Asia, Europe, and North America.
    {Lichen|Blaze}^[(Base == "White") && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Phlyctis petraea (eggshell rock blaze). White lichen growing on rock. Found in eastern North America.
    //Phylloblastia
    Lichen^[(Base == "Black" && Agouti == "Tabby" && Rufous != "High" && Gold == "None" && !Silver) && (NorthAm || Europe)]
      desc = Phylloblastia fortuita. Grey lichen growing in weblike structures on leaves. Found in Western Europe and North America.
    //Phyllopsora
    Lichen^[(Base == "White" || Base == "Cream") && (NorthAf || SouthAf || Islands)]
      desc = Phyllopsora dolichospora. Pale yellow lichen. Found across East Africa (including Tanzania), Mauritius, the Seychelles, and Sri Lanka.
    Lichen^[((Base == "Blue" || Base == "Lilac") && (White == "NoWhite") && (Albino == "Normal" || Albino == "Sepia")) && (NorthAm || MidAm || SouthAm || EastAs || SEastAs || Islands)]
      desc = Phyllopsora pyxinoides. Blue-green leafy lichen growing on bark. Widely distributed in Brazil. It has also been found in Colombia, in mainland Ecuador, Mexico, and Florida. Outside of the Americas, the lichen has been reported from South and Southeast Asia, including India, Sri Lanka, and Thailand.
    //Physcia
    Lichen^[(Base == "Black" && (Agouti != "Tabby" || Silver) && (White == "HighWhite" || White == "MidWhite")) && (NorthAm || MidAm || SouthAm || Europe || British || NorthAf || SouthAf || WestAs || EastAs || Japan || Australia || NewZeal || Islands)]
      desc = Physcia aipolia (Hoary rosette lichen). Black and white lichen growing on bark. Found nearly worldwide.
    Lichen^[(Base == "White" || ((Base == "Lilac" || Base == "Blue") && (White == "HighWhite" || White == "MidWhite"))) && (NorthAm || SouthAm || Europe || British || NorthAf || SouthAf || WestAs || EastAs || Japan || Australia || NewZeal || Islands || Antarctica)]
      desc = Physcia caesia (blue-gray rosette lichen, powder-back lichen). White & pale grey lichen growing on rock. Widely distributed across Europe, as well as in Greenland, and Britain. Though found across much of North America, it is absent from central and southeastern United States, parts of the Great Basin, and northern Alaska. In South America, it is found in Argentina, Chile, and Peru. It occurs patchily across Asia—in India, Bhutan, Nepal and Japan—as well as in East Africa. It is described as "cosmopolitan" in New Zealand, has been reported from a number of sites in southeastern Australia and Tasmania, and also occurs in Antarctica.
    Lichen^[(Base == "White" || ((Base == "Black") && (White == "HighWhite"))) && (NorthAm || Europe || Islands)]
      desc = Physcia magnussonii. White, branching lichen with black tips, growing on rock. Found in Northern and Central Europe, and Greenland. In North America, it has been recorded in Washington, Oregon, and Idaho southwards to Colorado.
      Lichen^[(Base == "Green" && (White != "Highhite") && (Albino == "Normal")) && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Physcia millegrana (mealy rosette lichen). Light green lichen growing on bark. It is common in the eastern United States.
    Lichen^[(Base == "White" || ((Base == "Black") && (White == "HighWhite" || (Silver && Agouti != "Solid" && Tabby == "Spotted")))) && (NorthAm || Europe)]
      desc = Physcia stellaris (fringed rosette lichen). White lichen with black spots, growing on rock. Found all across the temperate zones of North America as well as parts of Europe.
    //Physciella
      Lichen^[(Base == "Green" && (White == "NoWhite") && (Albino == "Normal")) && (NorthAm || Europe || EastAs || Japan)]
      desc = Physciella chloantha. Green lichen. The lichen's distribution includes diverse regions, from the Upper Midwest of the US to parts of Europe and Japan, Pakistan, and European Russia.
    //Piccolia
    Lichen^[(((Base == "Red" && Rufous == "Low") || (Base == "Cream" && Rufous == "High")) && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm)]
      desc = Piccolia nannaria. Yellow-green lichen growing on bark. Found in the coastal plain of southeastern North America, south to Georgia, to as far north as Maryland.
    //Pilophorus
    Lichen^[(Base == "Black" && Agouti == "Tabby" && Rufous != "High" && Gold == "None" && !Silver && Tabby == "Spotted" && White == "NoWhite" && Albino == "Normal") && (NorthAm || Japan || EastAs || Islands)]
      desc = Pilophorus acicularis (nail lichen, devil's matchstick lichen). Lichen growing as green stalks with spherical black tips. Have been found on the west coast of North America as far north as Alaska, but is most frequent in British Columbia and Washington. Found in China, Japan, and Taiwan, the Russian arctic.
    //Placidium
    {Lichen|Stipplescale}^[(Base == "White" || (Base == "Green" && (White == "NoWhite") && (Albino == "Normal"))) && (NorthAm || SouthAm)]
      desc = Placidium arboreum (tree stipplescale). Creamy white lichen growing in scale-esque patches, becoming green when wet. Found across North America, as well as the West Indies and Tucumán, Argentina.
    //Placocarpus
    Lichen^[(Base == "White" || Base == "Cream") && (Europe || WestAs)]
      desc = Placocarpus schaereri. White lichen growing on rock in schaly sheets. Found in Europe and West Asia.
    //Placomaronea
    Lichen^[(((Base == "Red" && Rufous == "Low") || (Base == "Cream" && Rufous == "High")) && (White == "NoWhite") && Albino == "Normal") && (SouthAm)]
      desc = Placomaronea candelarioides. Lichen growing as bright golden spots on rock. It is recorded along the Andes, from Mendoza (Argentina) north to Peru's Ancash region.
    //Placopsis
    Lichen^[((Base == "Red") && (White == "HighWhite" || Albino != "Normal")) && (Islands || Antarctica)]
      desc = Placopsis antarctica. White lichen with a golden-orange center growing on rock. Found in South Orkney Islands, South Shetland Islands, and the Antarctic Peninsula.
